    "notes": "Method: I read every fold screenshot directly. For the tall -full PNGs I cropped them into 1,500px slices with a small pure-Python PNG decoder, because the full images downscale too far to read. The slices are in /tmp/claude-1000/-home-agentops-dev-md-manager/541817b2-200f-49c5-b924-e4e11cf0112a/scratchpad/ux/work/ (e.g. 06-04500.png means launch page y 4,500-6,000), and the script is work/crop.py. Page heights come from the PNG headers; y positions are read from the slices at 1440px width and are approximate (±30px). Nothing in the repo was edited, and no tests or servers were run.\n\nThe live API was used read-only: 4 workflows, each with exactly 1 run, all named 'Feature implementation'. results/game/1 and /2 for skeleton-001 return 200 with the failed attempts' checks and error, so earlier attempts can be shown without backend work.\n\nRoot cause for the naming problem: workflow/export_state.py:84 returns {\"name\": \"Feature implementation\", …}.\n\nConstraints for redesign (testids pinned by tests/project-workflows/*.spec.ts): run-node-list with [data-node-id] children (lanes, guardrails, projects specs); graph-legend with 3 li carrying data-executor (clarity.spec.ts:105-109); node-status-meaning containing 'not workflow completion' (projects.spec.ts:172); node-hint (projects.spec.ts:162,179); projects-info containing 'Read-only' (projects.spec.ts:81); reuse-none/reuse-list and node-events/events-none must be visible (projects.spec.ts:232-256); file-findings-none exact text (clarity.spec.ts:268); tab-assignment/tab-run; run-inputs-facts (7 uses). A compacted design can keep these testids on smaller elements, such as tooltips or collapsed sections, but tests asserting toBeVisible will need updating if content moves behind disclosures.\n\nTruthfulness intent from the earlier slices to preserve in compact form: executor marks (PRD_VIEWER_CLARITY §4.3), 'worker succeeded ≠ workflow complete', and the read-only / CLI-only actions.\n\nSuggested IA direction, one page per question:\n- Runs home (all projects): runs newest first, with feature title, status, current or failed step, age, duration and a needs-you flag.\n- Run page: a 'Now' banner (step, reason, next command), a timeline with durations, a compact fitted graph, and collapsed run details.\n- Node view: full width, sticky step strip with prev/next, sub-tabs with counts (Overview/Checks/Screenshots/Files/Findings/Questions/Task/Events), and an attempt switcher.\n- Assignment: routed, per lane, decisions collapsed.\n\nBackend asks, collected:\n1. Feature title as definition.name, or a feature_title field.\n2. An attention field on RunSummary (waiting questions, awaiting approval, failed node).\n3. A copyable next-step command, or the unredacted run path.\n4. Per-node attempt result URIs.\n5. Controller event fixes: review events for print transport, PID checkpoint as a node-less log, and a reason on candidate failure events."
