    "questions_by_page": "PROJECTS LIST (01). Is anything running right now? Which project had activity most recently? First screen: NO. Only names and IDs, with no status or time.\n\nPROJECT (02). Which feature or workflow ran last, and how did it end? Is one running? First screen: NO. Two identical 'Feature implementation' cards show only revision hashes, with no run time or status.\n\nWORKFLOW RUN LIST (03, 03-mobile).\n- When did the latest run start and end, and how long did it take? PARTIAL: absolute UTC created/updated only, no duration, and 'updated' is not last activity.\n- Did it pass, and where did it stop? PARTIAL: a status badge only, no failing node or failure time.\n- Is it live, and when did it last change? NO: no relative time and no freshness indicator.\n\nRUN PAGE (04, 09, 13; mobile 04).\n- What is active right now? PARTIAL: graph colours only, no 'running for Xm'.\n- When did it fail or go idle, and what happened most recently? NO: 'Updated 09:36:07 UTC' is 3.5 minutes after the last activity, and 'Last event: sequence 26' is a number.\n- How long did each step take, and the total? NO: no durations anywhere.\n- What is the chronology of retries, repairs and controller resumes? NO: there is no run timeline, and node_id-null events (repair, diagnosis, resumes) are never rendered.\n- Is a worker waiting on a question, and since when? NO: this is only visible deep inside the launch node.\n- Are times in my timezone? NO: UTC only.\n\nNODE PAGES.\n- Challenge (05). When did each attempt run, how long did it take, and why was it retried? NO in the first screen. Events are at ~1,950 of 3,655px, all mislabelled 'attempt 1', with no durations. Earlier attempts' concerns are not viewable.\n- Launch worker (06). When did the worker start, how long has it worked or did it work, what is the deadline, when did it signal completion or stop? NO. The launch receipt, stop line and events are at ~19,300-19,800px of a 19,834px page. Elapsed time, deadline and completion time are not shown, and the observed state 'working' is stale.\n- Handoff (12). How long did we wait for the worker? NO. Only the freeze instant is shown, although the page fits in one screen.\n- Verify (07, 07-mobile). Which attempt failed when, how long did checks and setup take, and what changed between attempts? NO. Check ranges are at ~3,100px, events at ~4,400px (desktop) and ~8,800px (mobile). There are no durations, and earlier attempts' results are not linked even though the API serves them.\n- Candidate (11). When did it start, how long did it take, and which lane failed when? NO. There is no start event, check ranges are below the fold, and in the two-lane run the lane-less flipping events are confusing.\n- Review (08 print, 10 native). When did review start, how long did each reviewer take, and when was the verdict? PARTIAL. 'Reviewed at' and the reviewer launch and accept times are just below the fold. The print review has 'No events reference this node' and no launch times, and there are no durations or deadline.\n- Approval/Integrate. When was it approved or integrated? Approval: NO ('No events'). Integrate: one event at the bottom.\n\nASSIGNMENT TAB (14). How much time was the worker given, and what were the timeouts? YES: timeouts per check and setup and deadlines are listed. It carries no chronology, which is fine for its purpose.",
    "notes": "TIMESTAMP INVENTORY (what the API exposes → where the UI renders it today):\n- summary.created_at/updated_at → run header 'Created/Updated' (RunView.tsx:99-100) and run list card (ProjectsView.tsx:203). updated_at = max(export updated_at, last event time) (server/projects.ts:936), so it can trail activity.\n- snapshot.last_sequence → 'Last event: sequence N' (no time or message).\n- events[].occurred_at (+ node_id, attempt, status, message) → only 'Events for this node' at the bottom of NodeDetail (NodeDetail.tsx:466-487), reuse rows (:351) and approval rows (:385; never populated). node_id null events are never shown.\n- inputs.workers[].launch.launch_requested_at/native_started_at → Launch receipt (WorkerInputs.tsx:139-140), bottom of the launch node.\n- inputs.workers[].stop.confirmed_at → 'Stop confirmed at' line under the launch node's events (WorkerInputs.tsx:351).\n- inputs.workers[].questions[].asked_at/answered_at → WorkerQuestions (WorkerInputs.tsx:282/288), deep in the launch node.\n- inputs.challenge.decided_at → Challenge 'Decided' (Challenge.tsx:49); attempts/attempt count only.\n- inputs.automatic.worker_timeout_seconds/review_timeout_seconds, setup[].timeout_seconds, checks[].timeout_seconds → 'Deadlines' / timeouts only (never turned into a deadline clock).\n- results checks[].started_at/finished_at → 'start → finish' per check (NodeDetail.tsx:197), no duration.\n- reviews reviewers[].launched_at/accepted_at, reviewed_at → reviewer strip (ReviewDetail.tsx:158-159), 'Reviewed at' (:244).\n- NOT in the API: completion signalled_at, observed_state observed_at, per-attempt challenge records, print reviewer launch times, approval decision time, verify setup timing, candidate start, a run 'last_activity_at', and structured lane/attempt on events.\nEvery rendered time goes through formatTime → full-date UTC with seconds (status.ts:100). Nothing is relative or local, and formatDuration is used only for configured timeouts.\n\nA TIMELINE THAT CAN BE BUILT PURELY FROM EXISTING DATA (skeleton-001 as the example; times in UTC here, local in the UI):\nHeader: 'Failed at Independent review · 09:32 (blocked by general, 1 P1) · ran 56m (08:39→09:32) · last activity 09:32'.\nPhase bar: Challenge 11m07s (3 attempts) | Worker game 28m21s | Handoff instant | Verify 10m01s (3 attempts incl. 5m37s operator repair) | Candidate ≈1m06s | Review ≈2m10s ✗.\nRows: 08:39:42 Challenge attempt 1 started · 08:45:55 re-pinned → attempt 2 · 08:46:41 attempt 2 interrupted (KeyboardInterrupt, 46s) · 08:48:20 attempt 3 · 08:50:49 passed (2m29s, 8 P2) · 08:50:52 worker game started (native) · 08:50:55 controller resumed · [gap 28m: worker working] · 09:19:13 worker stopped, snapshots frozen · 09:19:13 verify attempt 1 → 09:20:20 failed (1m07s; unit/integration: no test evidence) · 09:20:23 attempt 2 → 09:21:30 failed (1m07s) · 09:21:32 DIAGNOSIS 'failed identically… lane repair (RUNBOOK)' · [gap 5m37s: operator] · 09:27:09 Repair 1 by operator (reporter for Vitest) · 09:28:00 controller resumed, attempt 3 → 09:29:15 passed (1m15s: setup 42s + checks 33s) · 09:29:41–09:30:21 candidate checks passed · ≈09:30:21 review started (inferred) · 09:32:31 general blocked (1 P1), coverage superseded → run failed.\nDerivation rules: node span = first→last status event, or dependency end → reviewed_at/stop.confirmed_at when events are missing (label these 'inferred'). Attempt spans come from events once the lowercase 'attempt' parse is fixed. Worker span = native_started_at→stop.confirmed_at. Question wait = asked_at→answered_at or now. Worker deadline = native_started_at + worker_timeout_seconds + question waits. Reviewer deadline = launched_at + review_timeout_seconds. Gaps over about 2 minutes between events become labelled gap rows. Earlier verify attempts link to .../results/{lane}/{n} (verified live: game/1 and game/2 return 200).\n\nBACKEND GAPS (events or fields needed for full fidelity):\n1. Print-transport review: no events and reviewers[].launched_at null. The controller should log launch/verdict per print job.\n2. Approval: no event when it succeeds (automatic finish or CLI). It should log the decision and the actor.\n3. Candidate: no 'running' event, and per-lane events are aliased to 'candidate' without the lane.\n4. The controller-process raw node 'controller' collides with a lane named 'controller' (server/projects.ts:341-347 vs :1116).\n5. Attempt parsing is case-sensitive (server/projects.ts:1067-1069). The server-side fix is cheap, but a structured attempt and lane on raw events is better.\n6. Worker completion has no signalled_at, and launch.observed_state has no observed_at.\n7. Earlier challenge attempts (challenge-<n>.json) are not served, including a paused attempt's P0/P1 concerns.\n8. Verify packet lacks setup started/finished.\n9. No run-level terminal event ('run failed at node X'). A last_activity_at distinct from export rewrite time would make the header honest.\n10. Event types approval_requested/result_reused/result_published are declared in the contract but never produced by normalizeEvents (server/projects.ts:1087), so the UI sections that depend on them are always empty.\n\nMETHOD: I read every screenshot. The tall ones were cropped with a small Node PNG cropper written to scratchpad/ux/work/crop.cjs; crops are 06-a/06-z, 07-a/b/c, 08-a/b, 10-a/b and 11-a. I read all API JSON payloads, derived spans with a script, and made one read-only GET to confirm that earlier attempt results (results/game/1 and results/game/2) are served. No repo files were changed.\n\nTESTS: The UTC strings are pinned in tests/project-workflows/inputs.spec.ts:143-155 and guardrails.spec.ts:56/222/231. The test ids node-events and events-none are asserted in projects.spec.ts:232. A timeline redesign should keep these ids on the per-node filtered view, or update those tests.\n\nOVERLAP: questions-wait-time-buried and live-freshness-unknown also belong to other lenses. They are included here only for their time and recency angle."
