    "name": "Run Story: a timeline-first workflow viewer",
    "thesis": "A run happens in time, so the run page shows it in time order. The first screen answers three things at a glance:\n1. A **Now banner**: where the run is or where it stopped, why, since when, and the CLI command to run next.\n2. A **Steps strip**: the pinned graph as status chips with durations. It fits the page width, so there is no inner horizontal scroll.\n3. A **Run timeline**: every step attempt, retry, repair, controller restart, question and idle gap, with local times and durations. This includes the events with no node (node_id null) that the viewer hides today.\n\nEach timeline row opens a full-width node view. The view starts with the node's own verdict, timing and tries. Its evidence sits behind a section index with counts (Checks 5 · Screenshots 2 · Files 77 · Findings 4 …), instead of one column up to 20,000px tall.\n\nAlmost everything comes from data the run page already loads (events, snapshot, inputs, review) through one pure `buildTimeline()`. Three small server additions add status to the list pages, make run paths copyable, and fix how events are projected.",
    "information_architecture": "## Levels and routes\nThe app's history keeps only the pathname (`App.tsx:159` writes only the pathname; `navigatePathname` uses the same). So every view that should be linkable gets a path segment, not a query parameter. In `routes.ts`, the `run` level gets two fields: `view: 'timeline' | 'assignment'` and `attempt: number | null`.\n\n| Route | Page | What it answers first |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/projects` | **Runs home** | Does anything need me, what is running, what finished recently? Sections: *Needs you*, *Running*, *Recent* (all projects, newest first), then compact project cards. The read-only note stays here only (`projects-info`, projects.spec:81). |\n| `/projects/<p>` | Project | The same run rows for this project only, grouped by feature. The heading is the feature title (or the `workflow_id` slug until B1 lands). \"Feature implementation\", node count and revision become secondary text. |\n| `/projects/<p>/workflows/<w>` | Feature runs | Run rows (`run-list`). \"Current definition\" moves into a closed `<details>` below. |\n| `/…/runs/<r>` | **Run, Timeline tab** (default) | Header line → Now banner → Steps strip → Timeline. |\n| `/…/runs/<r>/assignment` | Run, Assignment tab (now routed) | What the run was asked to do. |\n| `/…/runs/<r>/nodes/<n>` | **Node view**, latest try | The node's verdict, timing, tries and next step; evidence behind the section index. |\n| `/…/runs/<r>/nodes/<n>/attempts/<k>` | Node view, try k | Try k's own result (served today as `results/<lane>/<k>`). |\n\n## Run page, top to bottom\n1. **Header line** (`run-view`)\n   - First line: run id, status badge, feature title (`inputs.feature`), and a LiveStatus pill.\n   - Subline: `feature/skeleton/skeleton-001 @ 313eb87 · automatic · 08:39 → 09:32 · 52m51s` and a `Details ▸` disclosure (`run-details`).\n   - The disclosure holds everything from today's 11-fact grid: `pinned-definition` and `run-inputs-facts` (deadlines, permission mode, finish, mode, base commit, branch).\n   - `definition-changed` stays visible as a warning chip, and only when the pinned definition revision differs from the current one.\n2. **Now banner** (`run-now`). Contents: focus step, reason, time and age, a one-line honesty clause (`run-status-meaning`), and the likely next command with a Copy button.\n3. **Steps strip.** One HTML `<ol>` carries both `workflow-graph` and `run-node-list`.\n   - Columns and rows come from `layoutDag()`.\n   - Each chip is an `<a data-graph-node data-node-id data-status data-executor>` link.\n   - Edges are drawn in an `aria-hidden` SVG overlay that keeps `data-edge-from` and `data-edge-to`.\n   - A one-line legend follows (`graph-legend`, 3 `li`).\n4. **Tabs.** Timeline | Assignment. They are links with `role=tab` and `aria-selected`, and keep the testids `tab-run` and `tab-assignment`.\n5. **Timeline** (`run-timeline`). A time axis, the rows, a caption (`node-hint`: \"Oldest first · select a step to open its evidence\"), a Local/UTC toggle, and a \"Controller log (n)\" toggle.\n\nThe node panel, \"Select a node…\", the keyboard hint and both footnotes are removed from this page.\n\n## Node view (full width; replaces the timeline area)\n- **Sticky bar:** `‹ Timeline`, the Steps strip (compact; dots at 760px and below), and `‹ Prev · Next ›` in definition order.\n- **Header** (`node-detail`): label, status, executor word (`node-executor`), `try n of N` (`node-attempt` keeps the bare number), and a timing line (`node-timing`: start → end · duration · where the times came from).\n- It also shows a one-line outcome and a short `node-status-meaning`. When this node is the run's focus, it repeats the next command.\n- **Try strip** (`node-attempts`): one chip per try, with time, duration and the first reason. Repair markers sit between tries.\n- **Section index** (`section-index`): in-page links with counts. Empty sections get no chip and are not rendered.\n\nSections by node kind:\n- **launch_<lane>:**\n  1. Questions (first, and highlighted, when one waits)\n  2. Worker report (completion, clamped to 3 lines)\n  3. Files (dense rows; findings first; collapsed)\n  4. Task (closed, but the finding-highlight flow opens it)\n  5. Session (identifiers and receipts, closed)\n  6. History\n- **verify_<lane>:**\n  1. Gate (reasons mapped to checks)\n  2. Checks table\n  3. Screenshots (thumbnails)\n  4. Other artifacts (closed)\n  5. A \"Worker's report → Launch <lane> worker\" link\n  6. History\n- **candidate:**\n  1. Lane table, failing lanes first; a lane expands to its gate, checks and screenshots\n  2. History\n- **review:**\n  1. Verdict with blocking-finding cards\n  2. Reviewers (with durations)\n  3. Findings (existing grouping and filter)\n  4. Diff\n  5. History\n- **challenge:**\n  1. Outcome (\"Passed on try 3 · 8 P2 notes\")\n  2. Concerns, one line each; P0/P1 open by default\n  3. History\n- **handoff, approval, integrate:** an outcome line (integrate adds the commit and branch), then History.\n\n## What moves where\n| Item | Today | New home |\n|---|---|---|\n| 11 run facts | Grid at y≈200–490 (RunView.tsx:98-131), 7 of them repeated in Assignment (Assignment.tsx:31-44) | One header subline plus the closed `Details` disclosure. The duplicates are removed from Assignment. |\n| Failing step and reason | Review node y≈1,113; lane error nested in candidate | Now banner and the timeline row's outcome |\n| Next CLI command | Buried in event #20 (verify_game y≈4,600) | Now banner, and the header of the node that is the run's focus |\n| Run history, including node_id-null events | Per node, at the bottom; node-less events never shown | Timeline tab |\n| Node list | Left 1/3 column (App.css:345) | The Steps strip (same `run-node-list` testid) |\n| 1,680px SVG graph and legend | Run page and workflow page | Fitted Steps strip on the run page; closed \"Current definition\" on the workflow page |\n| Worker questions | Launch node, y≈19,320 | Now banner, a `?` badge on the strip chip, a Needs-you row, first section of the launch node |\n| 77 changed files | 15,400px of panels | Files section: rows, \"With findings (3)\" first, content on demand |\n| Worker summary and assumptions | Launch ×2, verify ×1 | Launch node Worker report, once; links everywhere else |\n| Checks | Verify node, y≈2,480, one ~125px card each | Checks table at the top of verify, with durations |\n| Earlier tries | Unreachable | Try strip and `/attempts/<k>` |\n| Launch receipt, stop line, session ids | Bottom of the launch node | Timing line plus the Session disclosure |\n| Worker task | Assignment and launch node | Launch node Task (keeps the requirement-highlight flow) plus a closed per-lane entry in Assignment |\n| Assignment tab | Component state (RunView.tsx:50) | `/runs/<r>/assignment`. Order: lanes table, then decisions (closed, with a heading outline), then setup. |\n| Breadcrumb | Home / Projects / p / Feature implementation / run | Projects / p / <feature title or slug> / run ● / <node label> |\n| App subtitle on Projects pages | Pi/Claude containment text (App.tsx:635) | \"Workflow runs — read-only\" |",
