ate matches require the code…” [game task ›]│\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\nLikely next step — findings after review are fixed in a new run (RUNBOOK · Automatic mode: the review step)\n$ python -m workflow launch <new-feature> --automatic --live                            [Copy]\nReviewers  general ✗ blocked · 4 findings · verdict 09:32:31   coverage — superseded when the run was decided\n[Findings 4 · 1 blocking] [Diff] [History 0]\n── Findings (4) ── Group: (Disposition) (Worker) (Reviewer)   Reviewer: All ▾   [?]\n   Table at 761px and wider, with single-value columns (Worker = game) hidden; cards at 760px and narrower.\n── History ── No events were recorded for this review (print transport). Verdict recorded 09:32:31.\n```\nFor a native review (skeleton-fixes-001), the reviewer line reads `general ✓ 3m49s · coverage ✓ 2m04s`.\n\n## 5. Run page at 390px (first screen, then the node view)\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ MD Manager                 [Refresh] │\n│ (Pi) (Claude) (Projects)             │\n│ ‹ skeleton / skeleton-001            │\n├──────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ skeleton-001  ✗ Failed               │\n│ Pirate Sea Race walking skeleton     │\n│ 08:39 → 09:32 · 52m51s   [Details ▸] │\n│ ● Finished · not polling             │\n│┌ NOW ───────────────────────────────┐│\n││ ✗ Stopped at Independent review    ││\n││ 09:32 · 2 h ago                    ││\n││ Blocked by general: 1 P1 — Private ││\n││ matches can be joined without their││\n││ code                     [Open ›]  ││\n││ Next: fix in a new run (RUNBOOK)   ││\n││ $ python -m workflow launch …      ││\n││ [Copy]                             ││\n│└────────────────────────────────────┘│\n│ ●─●─●─●─●─✗─○─○                      │\n│ Step 6 of 8 · Independent review     │\n│ [Timeline] [Assignment]              │\n│ 08:39 ? Design challenge · try 1     │\n│       ended without a record · 6m13s │\n│       ▆▆                             │\n│ 08:45 ✗ Design challenge · try 2     │\n│       interrupted · 46s              │\n└──────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\nTapping a row opens the node view:\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ ‹ Timeline  ●─●─●─◉─●─✗─○─○   ‹  ›  │  <- sticky, 44px targets\n│ Verify game  ✓ Succeeded · try 3 of 3│\n│ 09:28 → 09:29 · 1m15s                │\n│ Gate passed; build, browser at cand. │\n│ Tries #1✗ #2✗ ⚒ #3✓                  │\n│ [Checks 5][Shots 2][History 7]       │\n│ ✓ typecheck · 3s            [Log ▸]  │\n│ …                                    │\n└──────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\nOpening a node scrolls to the top and focuses its heading, so the detail is never 2,000px down. Returning to the timeline puts focus back on the originating row. The page has no horizontal overflow: `overflow-wrap: anywhere` is set on `.node-detail`, and the findings and checks become cards at 760px and narrower.",
    "timeline": "**Model.** `src/projects/timeline.ts` exports a pure `buildTimeline({ definition, snapshot, events, inputs, review, now })`. It returns:\n\n```\n{\n  runStart,\n  runEnd | null,\n  spans: Span[],       // one per node try: nodeId, label, kind, attempt, attemptsOf, start, end, startSource, endSource, status, outcome, live\n  markers: Marker[],   // diagnosis | repair | controller | controllerError | question | answer | log, with a time and the humanized message\n  gaps: Gap[],         // from, to, ms, kind: operator | controllerDown | idle\n  byNode: Map<nodeId, Span[]>\n}\n```\n\nIt is unit-tested with trimmed copies of the three live payloads. The run page already loads everything it needs:\n- `events[]`: sequence, occurred_at, node_id, attempt, status, message.\n- `snapshot.nodes[]`: status, attempt, result_uri, lane_results.\n- `definition.nodes[]`: label, kind, depends_on (used to infer start times).\n- `inputs.workers[]`:\n  - `launch.native_started_at` / `launch_requested_at`\n  - `stop.confirmed_at`\n  - `questions[].asked_at` / `answered_at`\n  - `completion.status`\n- other `inputs` fields:\n  - `challenge.attempts` and `decided_at`\n  - `max_verification_attempts`\n  - `automatic.worker_timeout_seconds` and `review_timeout_seconds`\n- One review result, fetched only once the review node is no longer pending: reviewed_at, reviewers[].launched_at / accepted_at / status.\n- The node view adds `checks[].started_at` / `finished_at` from the result it already loads, for the setup-versus-checks split.\n\n**Derivation rules** (each rule carries a source tag, which is shown in the tooltip):\n1. **Try number.** Re-read the try from the message with `/\\battempt (\\d+)/i` before falling back to `event.attempt`. The server's parser only matches a capital \"Attempt\" (`server/projects.ts:1068`), which is why every challenge event says \"attempt 1\" today.\n2. **Controller noise.** A message matching `Automatic checkpoint controller PID N` is a controller marker wherever it lands. In guardrails it lands on `launch_controller` as \"running\" (see B4). A `[Errno …]` failure on a node that later succeeded is a controller-error marker.\n3. **Spans.** A `running` event opens a span for that node and try. A terminal status (succeeded, failed, paused, cancelled) closes it. A new try opening while one is still open closes the old one as \"ended without a record\": challenge try 1, 08:39:42 → 08:45:55.\n4. **Receipts.**\n   - Worker spans use `native_started_at` → `stop.confirmed_at` (08:50:52 → 09:19:13 = 28m21s). The source is shown as \"from receipts\".\n   - A review without events uses `reviewed_at` as its end. Its start is the latest `launched_at`, otherwise the end of the step it depends on, marked \"≈ … inferred\" (09:30:21 → 09:32:31, ≈2m10s).\n   - A candidate without a running event starts at the end of the step it depends on (inferred): 09:29:15 → 09:30:21.\n   - An approval without events is an instant at the integrate event's time (inferred).\n5. **Run-level events** (node_id null).\n   - `failed identically` becomes a highlighted **diagnosis** row.\n   - `^Repair (\\d+)` becomes a **repair** row, with the snapshot and files from the node's paused event (#20).\n   - Anything else becomes a plain log row.\n6. **Gaps.** A stretch of more than 120 s with no open span becomes a gap row, classified by what surrounds it:\n   - after a diagnosis or failure and before a repair or resume: **operator time** (skeleton-001: 5m37s, 09:21:32 → 09:27:09)\n   - after controller errors and before a controller start: **controller not running** (guardrails-001: 19:33 → 19:34, 19:42 → 19:47, 19:48 → 19:55, 20:03 → 20:04)\n   - otherwise: **no activity**\n   A worker that is working is a span, not a gap.\n7. **Questions.** One row per `asked_at` (\"game asked question 2 · waited 5m\") and per `answered_at`. While `answer === null` the row is live (\"waiting 4m, deadline paused\"). If the export is stale, an `asked question N` event message without a later answer event serves as a fallback.\n8. **Run span.** It runs from `created_at` to the last non-controller activity, not to `updated_at`. For skeleton-001 the page shows 52m51s ending 09:32:31, instead of \"Updated 09:36:07\".\n\n**Display.**\n- Rows are `<li data-testid=\"timeline-row\" data-kind=\"span|marker|gap|question\" data-node-id data-attempt data-status>`. Span rows are links to `/nodes/<n>/attempts/<k>`. Each shows local clock time (HH:MM), a status glyph and word, the label, \"try k of N\", a one-line humanized outcome, a duration, and a bar.\n- The bar is a CSS track. Its left is (start − runStart)/total, its width is the duration/total, minimum 2px, and it is `aria-hidden`. Overlapping lanes show as parallel bars (guardrails: two workers from 19:32:57 to 20:08).\n- Inferred values show \"≈\" plus the source in a tooltip. Times use `<time dateTime title=\"2026-09-24 09:19:13 UTC\">`. A relative age is added when under 24 h or while the run is live.\n- A Local/UTC toggle is remembered per viewer in localStorage, wrapped in try/catch. It helps when matching events.jsonl.\n- Durations read `46s`, `2m29s`, `28m21s`, `1h05m`. Humanized messages shorten SHAs to 7 characters, and phrases are mapped, e.g. \"Awaiting explicit completion signal; idle is not acceptance\" → \"Waiting for the worker's completion signal (idle is not acceptance)\". The full message and sequence number are in the row's title and an expander.\n- The order is oldest first, with a remembered \"Newest first\" toggle. The live span sits at the end: its bar grows to now and it shows `working 12m · deadline 11:50 (2h38m left)`.\n- The controller-log toggle hides PID rows by default and shows their count.\n\n**Reuse on other surfaces.**\n- The Steps strip shows each node's total (first start → last end) and `↻n` when there were retries.\n- The run header shows the total.\n- Run rows show age and duration.\n- The node view's try strip is `byNode(nodeId)`, and its History section (`node-events`) is the same row component filtered to that node, plus the raw events behind an expander.\n- The verify header shows the setup/checks split: attempt start → first `check.started_at` → last `finished_at` (42s + 33s).\n- Reviewers show `accepted_at − launched_at` (general 3m49s, coverage 2m04s) and, while pending, time left against `review_timeout_seconds`.\n- \"Awaiting approval since 10:14 (12 min)\" uses the node's last status event.\n\n**Terms.** \"try k of N\" for verification and candidate, where N is `max_verification_attempts`. \"try k\" for the challenge. No try count on worker, handoff or pending nodes. \"Repair n\" for operator repairs. The phrasings \"Graph attempt\" and \"(graph node attempt is 1)\" are removed.",
    "live_and_next_action": "**Now banner** (`src/projects/NowBanner.tsx`, testids `run-now`, `now-reason`, `now-command`, `copy-command`). `deriveNow()` in `nextStep.ts` picks one situation, in this priority order:\n1. **Waiting on you: a question.**\n   - Triggers: `inputs.workers[].questions` has one with `answer === null`, or `completion.status === 'question'`, or an `asked question N` event with no later answer.\n   - Shows \"? game asked question 2 · 4 min ago · deadline paused\", the question text, and `python -m workflow answer \"$RUN\" game \"<your answer>\"`.\n   - The strip chip gets a `?` badge (`data-attention=\"question\"`), and the run row moves to *Needs you*.\n2. **Paused.**\n   - A challenge with a P0/P1: \"Paused: design challenge found 1 P1; no worker launched\". Commands: `python -m workflow resume \"$RUN\"` after revising the feature files, or `… resume \"$RUN\" --accept-challenge \"<reason>\"`.\n   - A repair or an interrupt: `python -m workflow automatic \"$RUN\" --live`.\n3. **Failed.** The focus is the failed node (the first in definition order, ties broken by the latest event).\n   - The reason comes from, in order: the review verdict plus blocking findings, the failing lane's `error.message` (the only case with extra fetches, one or two lane results, and only when the candidate failed), or the last status event message.\n   - Mapping:\n     - A diagnosis marker \"failed identically\" gives `python -m workflow repair \"$RUN\" <lane> --workspace`, then `python -m workflow automatic \"$RUN\" --live` (RUNBOOK \"Blocked after freeze: repair a lane\").\n     - A review block gives \"fixed in a new run\" and `python -m workflow launch <new-feature> --automatic --live` (RUNBOOK: \"after review started, create a new run\").\n     - A controller `[Errno …]` gives \"Controller could not run claude; fix the environment, then `automatic \"$RUN\" --live`\".\n     - Anything else gives \"No known next step matched\" plus a RUNBOOK section link. The viewer never guesses a command.\n4. **Awaiting approval.** \"Waiting for your approval since 10:14 (12 min)\" and `python -m workflow approve \"$RUN\" --bundle-sha256 <review.bundle_sha256>`. The hash is filled in from the review result.\n5. **Running.**\n   - Shows the active node or nodes: \"Launch duel worker · working 5m · deadline 14:12 (2h55m left)\". The deadline is `native_started_at + worker_timeout_seconds` + paused question time.\n   - Adds \"Last activity 11:13 (4 min ago): Waiting for the worker's completion signal\".\n   - Offers an optional attach command: `python -m workflow.interactive attach-one \"$RUN\" --node duel`.\n   - For a review, it shows per-reviewer elapsed time and time left.\n6. **Succeeded.** \"Integrated ee74298 into feature/skeleton-fixes/skeleton-fixes-001 · not pushed · 31m50s · review approved, 2 open P2 [view]\". The source is the integrate event plus `inputs.source_branch`. There is no workflow command, and pushing is left to the operator.\n7. **Cancelled or pending:** one plain line.\n\n**Commands.** Commands are always labelled \"Likely next step (from the RUNBOOK)\" and link to the RUNBOOK section. They use `\"$RUN\"`, the RUNBOOK's own convention.\n- With B3, a `RUN=<runs_root>/<run_id>` line with its own Copy button makes each command paste-ready.\n- Without B3, a small `What is $RUN?` disclosure explains \"the run directory: this workflow's runs_root/<run id> in the project registry\".\n- The honesty clause lives in one place, the banner: \"Run commands in your terminal; this viewer never changes a run\".\n- `run-status-meaning` becomes a short cause-aware clause that keeps the tested words: \"…The workflow did not complete.\" for failed, \"not complete until you approve it in the CLI\" for awaiting approval.\n- The Copy button's text is only \"Copy\" (its aria-label is \"Copy command\"). So `expectNoExecutionControls` (support.ts:36) still passes.\n- Clipboard failure falls back to selecting the `<code>`.\n\n**Focus node on node pages.** When the viewed node is the Now focus, its header repeats the reason and the command. The retryable wording (\"Marked retryable by the producer\") is replaced with \"try 2 of 3 · failed identically → repair\" when a diagnosis exists.\n\n**Liveness** (`LiveStatus.tsx`, `live-status`). `useResource` returns `meta { settledAt, lastError, inFlight }`, and `useNow(1000)` renders the ages. States:\n- \"● Live · updated 3 s ago\"\n- amber \"Not updating · showing data from 11:14:02 · retrying\" after a failed poll (today a failed poll is silent, useResource.ts:30-34)\n- \"Finished · not polling\" for succeeded or cancelled runs\n- \"Paused while this tab is hidden\"\n\nWith B1 it adds \"controller running (PID 3373084)\", or \"controller not running — the run will not advance\", which adds `automatic \"$RUN\" --live` to the Now banner.\n\n**Refresh.** Header Refresh becomes a background reload: `refreshToken` moves from useResource's `base` to its `token`, so the page no longer blanks, the scroll position and tab survive, and the pill shows \"Refreshing…\".\n\n**Announcements.** ProjectsView's existing polite region announces only changes of focus or status (\"skeleton-001: Verify game failed, try 2 of 3\"), not every tick.",
    "evidence_disclosure": "Evidence opens in four levels, and each level answers one question more.\n- **Level 0, run page:** one-line outcomes on the Now banner and on the timeline rows, e.g. \"unit, integration: no passing test evidence\" or \"blocked by general (1 P1)\".\n- **Level 1, node header:** status, try, timing and one outcome line, plus a section index whose counts tell the operator what exists before they scroll. Sections with nothing in them get no chip and no body. This replaces \"No reuse evidence…\", \"No review finding names this file\" repeated 77 times, and \"No artifacts beyond…\".\n- **Level 2, sections:** dense rows.\n- **Level 3, on demand:** logs, file contents, full-size screenshots, raw events, identifiers.\n\nRules by evidence type:\n- **Checks** (`checks-list`; each row keeps `.check` and `.check-exit` \"exit 0\").\n  - Each row shows a status glyph, the check id (matched by command against `inputs.workers[].checks`, as TaskPanel does), the command in truncated monospace, a +offset from the try's start, the duration, and a `Log ▸` toggle that opens the tail inline (the existing TextArtifact).\n  - The gate reasons in `error.message` are split on `; ` and matched to checks by their `<id>:` prefix. A matched check turns red: \"exit 0 · rejected by gate: …\" (`check-rejected`), and its log opens automatically. This covers `candidate_ui/2` in guardrails, where all three checks exited 0.\n  - The cwd, log artifact id and absolute times move to the row's tooltip.\n- **Screenshots** (`screenshots`): a thumbnail grid (`max-width: 220px`) captioned with the short artifact id. Clicking opens the full size in a `<dialog>` or the artifact URL. The sha256 goes to the tooltip. With B6, each caption shows the scenario id and its pass state.\n- **Files** (`created-files`, `changed-files`, `created-file`, `captured-file`).\n  - A \"With findings (n)\" filter comes first, then \"All (n)\", optionally grouped by folder. Each row shows the findings badge (e.g. \"P1 ×1\"), the capture state and an expander.\n  - Nothing is fetched until a row is opened, and Markdown files start closed. This fixes the eager fetch at CreatedFiles.tsx:454/461.\n  - An open row shows `file-findings` (or `file-findings-none`), the Source and Rendered toggles, and \"Show lines\".\n  - A finding link opens its row and scrolls to it (the existing `keepInView`).\n  - The list comes from the worker's own freeze (`results/<lane>/1`) when the latest result is a later try. Paths whose sha256 differs, or that exist only in the later result, get a \"repair 1\" badge.\n  - When `review.diff` exists, rows get A/M/D marks parsed from it, and the diff opens beside the full file.\n- **Worker narrative.** It appears only on the launch node: `worker-completion`, clamped to 3 lines with More, and its assumptions behind \"Assumptions (10) ▸\".\n  - If `result.summary` adds to the completion text, only the added part appears, as \"Verifier note: Operator repair 1 …\".\n  - Verify and candidate pages show a `worker-report-link` in its place. When two nodes share a `result_uri`, its facts appear once.\n- **Findings** (`review-findings`). Blocking findings (via `isBlockingFinding`) come first as cards, each with its file:line and requirement links.\n  - The table keeps its grouping and filter, and hides columns whose value is the same on every row.\n  - The four-line explanation moves behind a `[?]` disclosure.\n  - At 760px and narrower the table becomes cards, fixing the 560px `min-width` overflow.\n- **Questions** (`worker-questions`): first on the launch node and in the Now banner while one waits; otherwise a single line in the Session section.\n- **Task** (`task-details`): closed by default. The finding → requirement highlight flow still opens it.\n- **Session and receipts:** `launch-receipt`, the stop line (`worker-stop`), session ids and the base/output commit sit in a closed \"Identifiers & receipts\" disclosure. \"Observed state\" is relabelled \"State at launch\".\n- **Candidate lanes:** a table with lane, gate ✓/✗, checks n/n, first reason and screenshot count, failing lanes first and open. Each lane keeps `lane-result:<lane>`. The fixed boilerplate summary and \"No open assumptions\" are dropped.\n- **Other artifacts:** closed. A log that belongs to no check is labelled \"log (not a check log)\", because the viewer does not guess that it is the setup log.\n- **History** (`node-events` / `events-none`): the filtered timeline rows, plus \"Raw events (n)\" behind an expander.",
    "removed_or_demoted": "Removed from the run page:\n- The 11-fact grid moves into the closed `Details` disclosure.\n- \"Last event: sequence N\" is replaced by the last activity's message and age.\n- The fixed per-status sentence becomes the Now banner's cause-specific headline plus a short honesty clause.\n- The 1,680px SVG DAG (WorkflowGraph.tsx) is replaced by the fitted HTML Steps strip.\n- The 3-sentence executor legend becomes one line: \"▭ Agent session ┅ Trusted verifier ┈ Controller\", with the full wording in each item's tooltip and visually-hidden text.\n- The keyboard hint goes; the steps are ordinary links.\n- The duplicate Nodes column is merged into the strip, which keeps `run-node-list`.\n- The empty \"Select a node…\" panel goes (`node-hint` becomes the timeline caption).\n- The status-enum footnote goes (RunView.tsx:217).\n\nRemoved from node pages:\n- The \"Status labels here are historical observations…\" footnote (NodeDetail.tsx:488).\n- \"Reuse evidence\" goes unless `result_reused` events exist; the server never produces them today.\n- The 6-cell facts grid becomes one subline plus the Identifiers disclosure.\n- The Session id no longer repeats 3 times.\n- \"Depends on\" goes; the strip shows dependencies.\n- Worker summary and assumptions no longer repeat on verify and candidate pages.\n- \"Reported by the worker\" no longer repeats the result summary.\n- The per-file \"Findings on this file / No review finding names this file\" moves inside the opened file.\n- The gate's \"see the error above\" goes.\n- The \"Ownership:\" sentence is demoted to the gate tooltip.\n- \"Marked retryable by the producer\" goes.\n\nRemoved elsewhere:\n- The info line under the breadcrumb, except on /projects, where the read-only note is kept.\n- The \"Home\" breadcrumb, which pointed at the Pi/Claude area.\n- \"Feature implementation\" as the title of cards and breadcrumbs; it survives as secondary text only.\n- Revision hashes and node counts on cards.\n- The \"Current definition\" graph on the workflow page moves into a closed `<details>`.\n- The Pi/Claude subtitle in the app header on Projects pages.\n- Full UTC ISO timestamps become local HH:MM plus a relative age, with UTC in the tooltip and a toggle.\n\nDemoted but kept:\n- Honesty wording is said once, in the right place:\n  - worker success is covered by `node-status-meaning` on worker nodes: \"Session ended its turn. This is not workflow completion.\"\n  - read-only and CLI-only is one line in the Now banner\n  - \"as signalled by the session, not verified\" is a small tag on the worker report\n  - inferred times carry \"≈\" plus their source\n\nPartially addressed:\n- `no-diff-view`: A/M/D marks and diffs come only from `review.diff`; lanes that have no review yet would need B6 or a per-lane patch.\n- `artifacts-unlabeled`: the setup log is labelled only once B6 serves the labels.",
    "data_needs": "**Existing fields the redesign uses** (no change needed):\n- **Summary:** `summary.status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`.\n- **Definition:** `definition.nodes[]` (label, kind, depends_on).\n- **Snapshot:** `snapshot.nodes[]` (status, attempt, result_uri, lane_results).\n- **Events:** `events[]` (occurred_at, node_id including null, status, attempt, message).\n- **Inputs, run level:** `inputs.feature`, `base_commit`, `source_branch`, `automatic.*_timeout_seconds`, `max_verification_attempts`, `setup[]`, `challenge` (status, attempts, decided_at, concerns).\n- **Inputs, per worker:** `inputs.workers[]`:\n  - launch: `native_started_at`, `launch_requested_at`\n  - `stop.confirmed_at`\n  - `questions[]`\n  - `completion` (status, summary, question)\n  - `checks[]` (id ↔ command)\n- **Review:** `reviews/<n>` (verdict, findings, reviewers[].launched_at / accepted_at / status, reviewed_at, bundle_sha256, diff).\n- **Results:** `results/<lane>/<k>` for k from 1 up to the node's attempt, already served (the live API returns 200 for game/1 and game/2): checks[].started_at / finished_at / exit_code, error.message, artifacts, changed_files, deferred_checks.\n\nThe Now banner, the timeline, the try switcher, durations, the question banner on the run page, gaps and gate-reason mapping are all client-only.\n\n**Essential backend additions** (small, additive, no Python change):\n- **B4. Event projection fixes** in `server/projects.ts`, with no contract change.\n  - Make `attemptFromMessage` case-insensitive and let it match \"attempt N\" anywhere in the message (1067-1070).\n  - Make controller-process messages (`Automatic checkpoint controller PID`, supervisor interrupt, `[Errno`) run-level (`node_id` null) before lane aliasing. Today, in a run with a lane named `controller`, they are aliased onto `launch_controller` (341-347, 1116).\n  - Prefix lane-aliased candidate events with `[<lane>] `, so the timeline can say which lane failed.\n  - About 20 lines. The client applies the same heuristics until this lands.\n- **B1. An optional `activity` field on RunSummary**, with a contract bump for the summary:\n  ```\n  { feature, focus: {node_id, label, status} | null, reason: string | null (≤200 chars, redacted),\n    last_activity_at, finished_at, waiting_questions: number,\n    controller: { pid, alive: boolean | null } | null }\n  ```\n  - `listRuns` already runs `projectRun` for every run (server/projects.ts:788-813), so this costs no extra I/O. The one exception is `process.kill(pid, 0)` on the PID from the latest checkpoint event.\n  - It lets the run list, project page and Runs home show \"Failed at X · reason\", \"Waiting on you\", recency and \"controller not running\" without fetching events and inputs for each run.\n  - `waiting_questions` also counts `asked question N` events that have no later answer, so it is right while run-state.json is stale during the handoff wait.\n- **B3. Opt-in run directory.** A registry flag `workflows[].expose_run_dir: true` (in `projectsConfig.ts`) adds `run_dir` (runs_root/run_id) to RunDetail.\n  - The CLI needs the directory argument (pipeline.py:864, guardrails.py:939/998).\n  - Paths stay redacted by default (`redactPaths`, projects.ts:75). With the flag on, every command becomes copy-paste-ready.\n\n**Optional later:**\n- **B2.** `GET /api/projects/runs?limit=20` across the registry. Client fan-out works at today's scale (2 projects, 5 workflows); this avoids growing N+1 requests on /projects.\n- **B5. Controller and exporter** (Python):\n  - print-transport review start and verdict events, and `launched_at`\n  - an approval decision event with its actor\n  - a failure reason in candidate status events\n  - `completion.signalled_at`\n  - export questions during the wait loop\n  Until then the timeline labels these spans as inferred.\n- **B6.** Optional result fields `gate_reasons[{check_id, reason}]` and `evidence_checks[{id, tests, scenarios[{id, status, screenshot_artifact_id}]}]`, taken from the packet the server already reads (~1215-1235). These give exact rejected checks, test counts and screenshot captions by scenario.",
    "implementation": "**New files** (src/projects/):\n- `time.ts` plus `Time.tsx` (~120 LOC): `clock`, `relative`, `span`, `utcTitle`, `useNow`, and the Local/UTC preference. It replaces the 20 or so `formatTime` call sites.\n- `timeline.ts` (~350): `buildTimeline`, `humanizeEvent`.\n- `nextStep.ts` (~160): `deriveNow` and the table mapping each situation to its command.\n- `NowBanner.tsx` plus `CommandBlock.tsx` (~200).\n- `LiveStatus.tsx` (~60).\n- `StepStrip.tsx` (~220): replaces `WorkflowGraph.tsx`. It is an HTML grid built from `layoutDag`, with an SVG overlay for the edges and a dots mode at 760px and below.\n- `RunTimeline.tsx` (~260).\n- `NodeHeader.tsx`, `TryStrip.tsx`, `SectionIndex.tsx` (~300 together).\n- `Checks.tsx` (~180): the checks table and gate-reason mapping, moved out of `NodeDetail.tsx`.\n- `Screenshots.tsx` (~60).\n- `RunRow.tsx` (~120).\n\n**Changed files:**\n- `RunView.tsx`: rewritten, about the same size (~250).\n- `NodeDetail.tsx`: per-kind section order, empty sections hidden, duplicates removed; net about −100.\n- `CreatedFiles.tsx`: file rows, filter, lazy loading, repair badges (~+140).\n- `ReviewDetail.tsx`: headline cards, reviewer durations, cards at narrow widths (~+120).\n- `Challenge.tsx`: compact concerns (~−30).\n- `Assignment.tsx`: duplicate facts removed, lanes table, decisions closed (~+40).\n- `WorkerInputs.tsx`: question banner variant; `LaunchReceipt` moves into the Session disclosure.\n- `routes.ts`: `view` and `attempt` segments (~+40).\n- `ProjectsView.tsx`: breadcrumb, Runs home, grouped project page, RunRow (~+220).\n- `useResource.ts`: `meta`, and Refresh without blanking (~+25).\n- `status.ts`: shorter wording.\n- `App.tsx`: subtitle on Projects pages.\n- `App.css`: about +320 and −80 lines, in sections for header and Now, strip, timeline, node view and the 760px breakpoint. It adds status tokens in `index.css`, a distinct selection ring, and `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)` around the live pulse and smooth scrolling.\n\n**Server:**\n- `server/projects.ts`: B4 (~20), B1 (~80), B3 (~30).\n- `contracts/projects/v1.ts`: an optional `activity` and `run_dir` (~25).\n- `projectsConfig.ts`: the flag (~10).\n\n**Slice order** (each slice ships with its own tests and is useful on its own):\n1. **S1: time and freshness.** `Time`, relative times, the durations helper, `useResource` meta and Refresh without blanking, `LiveStatus`, and `timezoneId` in the Playwright config. Small, low risk, and it answers \"when\" at once.\n2. **S2: timeline model.** `timeline.ts` and `nextStep.ts`, pure, with unit tests on the three live payloads.\n3. **S3: run page.** Header line and Details, Now banner (client-only, using `$RUN`), StepStrip, RunTimeline, the routed Assignment tab, and the breadcrumb. The node route temporarily renders today's NodeDetail at full width with the sticky strip. This is the biggest win for the user: it fixes the first screen, the clipped graph, the wasted column and the mobile problem where the detail sat far below the fold.\n4. **S4: node view.** Header, timing, try strip with `/attempts/<k>`, section index, per-kind order, deduplication, checks table with gate rejections, thumbnails, and file rows (collapsed, repair badges).\n5. **S5: backend.** B4, B3, and B1 with the contract bump; the client switches to the served fields.\n6. **S6: lists.** RunRow on the workflow page, the project page grouped by feature, the Runs home (fan-out, then B2 if needed).\n7. **S7: polish.** Review cards and narrow tables, the candidate lane table, the compact challenge, the Assignment reorganisation, and A/M/D marks from `review.diff`.\n\nEstimated total: about 3,000 changed LOC.",
    "test_impact": "**Testids kept in place, or moved onto new elements with the same contract:**\n- **Steps strip:** `workflow-graph` and `run-node-list` sit on the strip's `<ol>`.\n  - The `li[data-node-id][data-status]` items stay in definition order (lanes.spec:67, guardrails.spec:92/145/311, projects.spec:40), and `nodeListItem(...).getByRole('link')` still works.\n  - `[data-graph-node]` moves onto the chip `<a>`, keeping `data-status` and `data-executor`.\n  - The `aria-label` keeps the exact format \"Label, kind, status, attempt n, executed by …\" (clarity.spec:96-99). The duration is attached with `aria-describedby`, so the anchored regexes still pass.\n  - `[data-edge-from][data-edge-to]` paths stay in the overlay SVG (lanes.spec:59-61).\n  - `graph-legend` keeps 3 `li[data-executor]` whose text still contains \"Agent session\", \"Trusted verifier\" and \"Controller\" (clarity.spec:105-109).\n- **Run page:** `node-hint` becomes the timeline caption and stays visible (projects.spec:162/179). `run-status` and `run-status-meaning` move into the Now banner and keep \"did not complete\" and \"not complete\".\n- **Node header:** `node-status-meaning` keeps \"This step failed\" and \"This is not workflow completion\".\n- **Unchanged:** `tab-run`/`tab-assignment` (with `aria-selected`), `definition-changed` (visible), `events-none`/`node-events` (visible History), `gate-outcome`, `deferred-checks`, `checks-list` `.check` / `.check-exit`, `screenshots`, `worker-completion`, `task-details`, all `review-*`, `finding*`, `group-by-*`, `filter-reviewer`, `lane-result:*`, `assignment*`, `run-list`, `workflows-list`, `projects-list`, `projects-info`.\n\n**Assertions that must change:**\n- `run-inputs-facts`, `pinned-definition` and `definition-current` now live in the closed `run-details` disclosure. `toContainText` still passes, because it reads textContent. The `toBeVisible` uses (inputs.spec:263, lanes.spec:56, projects.spec:184) must first click `run-details`.\n- `current-definition` is inside a closed `<details>` on the workflow page. `toContainText` passes; no change is needed.\n- `.workflow-node-meta` text (clarity.spec:101-103) becomes \"{duration}{ · ↻n} · {executor}\". Assert `toContainText('verifier')` and check `data-status` instead.\n- `node-attempt` for a pending node reads \"Not started\" instead of \"0 (not started)\" (projects.spec:302). The number stays for started nodes (projects.spec:211/298).\n- `reuse-none` is removed (projects.spec:233/256). Assert `reuse-list` `toHaveCount(0)` instead.\n- `worker-summary` and `assumptions` on a verify node (projects.spec:214/228) move to the launch node. The verify node asserts `worker-report-link`.\n- `worker-error` \"Retrying is done through the workflow CLI\" (projects.spec:305) is replaced by assertions on `gate-reason` and `now-command`.\n- UTC strings (inputs.spec:143-155; guardrails.spec:56 `shown()` and 222/231):\n  - Set `timezoneId: 'UTC'` and `locale: 'en-GB'` in `tests/project-workflows/playwright.config.ts` `use`.\n  - Assert `time[datetime=\"…\"]` or its `title`.\n  - The `worker-stop` text becomes \"Stopped 10:20\".\n- `launch-receipt` moves into the Session disclosure. `toContainText` works; any `toBeVisible` must open the disclosure first.\n- clarity.spec `created-file-rendered` (130-176) must open the Markdown row before `file-rendered`. `file-findings-none` (268) must open the file row first; its exact text is unchanged.\n- `output-first-task-collapsed` (177) still holds: the report and files come before the closed task.\n- `verify-shows-checks-not-files` (208) still holds.\n- The overflow checks at 420px (projects.spec:289, 323) must keep passing.\n- `expectNoExecutionControls` (support.ts:36): the Copy button's text must be \"Copy\", and no button text may contain a file path or command.\n\n**New tests:**\n- **Unit:** `tests/unit/timeline.test.ts` and `tests/unit/nextStep.test.ts`, run with `tsx --test` and added to `test:unit`. Fixtures are trimmed copies of skeleton-001, skeleton-fixes-001 and workflow-guardrails-001. They assert:\n  - try numbers re-read from the message (challenge tries 1–3)\n  - worker span 28m21s from the receipts\n  - diagnosis and repair rows, and PID rows collapsed\n  - the 5m37s operator gap\n  - the inferred review span ≈2m10s\n  - the guardrails controller gaps\n  - every `deriveNow` situation, including \"no step matched\"\n- **E2E** (add the scenario ids to the feature's `policy.json`):\n  - `[scenario:run-now-banner]`: the failed, succeeded and awaiting-approval banners, and the approve command carrying the bundle sha.\n  - `[scenario:run-timeline]`: row order and durations, node_id-null rows visible, the controller-log toggle, a row opening `/nodes/<n>/attempts/<k>`, and focus returning to that row on the way back.\n  - `[scenario:node-tries]`: try 1 loads `results/<lane>/1` and shows the rejected checks.\n  - `[scenario:waiting-question]`: a fixture with an unanswered question; banner, strip badge and launch node show Questions first.\n  - `[scenario:live-freshness]`: an aborted poll route turns `live-status` stale, and Refresh keeps the data on screen.\n  - `[scenario:narrow-run-focus]`: at 390×844, no horizontal overflow, and after selecting a step the node heading's box has `y` below 844.\n  - `[scenario:runs-home]`: Needs-you, Running and Recent grouping.\n- **Fixtures:** `tests/project-workflows/fixtures.ts` needs:\n  - null-node diagnosis, repair and PID events\n  - a question-waiting run\n  - a verify node at attempt 3 with results 1 to 3",
    "risks": "- **Inferred or heuristic times.** Some start times are inferred (review, candidate, approval), and parsing the try from message text is fragile. Mitigation:\n  - Every inferred value shows \"≈\" and its source.\n  - The heuristics live in one pure module with unit tests on the real payloads.\n  - B4 and B5 remove most of them later.\n  - A timeline row never claims more than the events do. An open span with no terminal event reads \"ended without a record\".\n- **Wrong next step.** A next-step suggestion could be wrong. Mitigation:\n  - It shows only when a situation from the table matches exactly; otherwise it says \"No known next step matched\" and links the RUNBOOK section.\n  - It is always worded \"Likely next step (from the RUNBOOK)\".\n  - The table in nextStep.ts is reviewed against the RUNBOOK and the CLI `--help` whenever the controller changes.\n- **Paths in commands.** Without B3, commands contain `\"$RUN\"`, which the operator must set. Exposing `run_dir` weakens the redaction policy, so it stays opt-in per workflow.\n- **Local times.** The CLI and events.jsonl are in UTC. Mitigation: every time's tooltip carries UTC, and a remembered Local/UTC toggle is available.\n- **Stale export during the handoff wait.** Mitigation: the question banner falls back to events, and B1 counts both sources. Fully live questions still need B5.\n- **Test churn.** About 15 assertions in 5 specs change, and scenario ids must be added to policy.json. Doing it slice by slice keeps each PR reviewable. Keeping testids on their new elements avoids a rewrite of the harness.\n- **Losing the SVG DAG.** An unusual DAG, for example with skip-level edges, could read less clearly in a column-grid strip. The overlay still draws every edge, and `layoutDag` stays the single source for columns.\n- **Re-renders.** Polling every 5 s re-renders the timeline on every tick. `buildTimeline` is memoized on the last event sequence plus the identities of the snapshot and inputs, and `useNow` ticks only while the run is live.\n- **Fan-out on /projects.** It grows as the number of workflows grows; B2 caps it.\n- **Changed UI habits.** The operator's links to `/nodes/<n>` keep working. Assignment and tries get new URLs, and the old routes still resolve.",
