    "angle": "triage-first",
    "name": "Answer-first run triage",
    "thesis": "Every Projects page should answer the operator's question in its top block, before it shows any evidence. A run page opens with a \"Now\" banner computed from existing data: the step where the run is or stopped, why in one line, when (local time plus how long ago), and the exact CLI command to run next with a Copy button. Below it come one card per lane (worker, verify, candidate, findings), then a step timeline with durations, which also serves as the node list. Deeper evidence (checks, logs, screenshots, files, findings, task) sits one click away in URL-addressable node tabs. One pure module, contracts/projects/triage.ts, does the classification and timing. The browser uses it first. The server reuses it later to give run lists the same headline, so the runs list becomes a dashboard sorted by what needs the operator.",
    "information_architecture": "## Levels and routes (all read-only)\n\n| Route | Answers first | Replaces / merges |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/projects` **Runs dashboard** | \"Does anything need me, what is running, what finished recently?\" Groups: **Needs you** (question, awaiting approval, paused, failed in the last 24 h), **Running**, **Recent**. Each row shows the feature title, run id, project, status glyph and word, the one-line headline (step + reason), last activity (relative), and duration. | Bare project cards (01). The project list stays below as compact links (`projects-list`, plus the \"Read-only\" line in `projects-info`). |\n| `/projects/<p>` **Project runs** | The same rows filtered to one project, grouped by feature. The group header (`workflows-list` link) reads \"Walking skeleton · skeleton · 1 run\". | Identical \"Feature implementation\" cards (02). |\n| `/projects/<p>/workflows/<w>` **Feature runs** | The run rows (`run-list`) with headline, duration and age. | The \"Current definition\" graph moves into a `<details>` that is open only when there are no runs. |\n| `/…/runs/<r>` **Run overview** (tab Run) | The Now banner, then lane cards, then the Steps timeline. | The 11-fact grid, the empty \"Select a node\" panel and the duplicate Nodes column. Facts move into a collapsed **Run details** disclosure. |\n| `/…/runs/<r>/assignment` (tab Assignment, now routed) | \"What was this run asked to do?\" A one-line setup summary, a lanes table (lane, role, required checks, owned-path count, link to the lane's Task tab), setup commands, and decisions.md collapsed with its heading outline. | The per-worker full task text moves to the launch node's Task tab. The Assignment tab keeps only run-level content, so nothing is duplicated. |\n| `/…/runs/<r>/nodes/<n>[/<section>]` and `/…/nodes/<n>/attempts/<k>[/<section>]` **Node view** | The node header: status, executor, start → end (duration), a one-line verdict, the next step when the node is failed, paused or waiting, and an attempt switcher. | The single long column. Sections become tabs with counts, and the tab and attempt live in the path (routes.ts gains `assignment`, `<section>` and `attempts/<k>` literals). |\n\n## Run overview, top to bottom\n1. **Title row**: feature title (h2), run id, status badge with an ⓘ popover (holds `run-status-meaning`), start → finish, duration, branch, and a LivePill (\"Live · updated 3 s ago\" / \"Connection lost · showing 11:14:02 · retrying\" / \"Finished · not polling\").\n2. **Now banner** (`run-now`): headline, reason, when, [Open step ›], and the Next step box (`next-step`).\n3. **Step map**: the existing SVG graph, fitted to the width. Each node gets a status glyph and its duration, and the legend shrinks to one short line of chips.\n4. **Lanes and gates** (`lane-card` per lane, plus a Review/Integration card).\n5. **Timeline** with a [Steps | Log] toggle. Steps is the ordered node list (`run-node-list`), one row per node in definition order, with start, duration bar, tries and a one-line outcome. Log shows every event, including run-level ones, with gap rows.\n6. **Run details** disclosure (`run-details`): `run-inputs-facts`, `pinned-definition`, definition changed/current, permission mode, finish policy and base commit.\n\n## Node view, top to bottom\nRun bar (one line: ← run, feature, status, Now one-liner \"Blocked at Independent review · Next step ›\", LivePill). Then the **sticky step chips** (`run-node-list` on node pages: one link per node with glyph, short label and duration, plus prev/next links). Then the **node header** (`node-detail`, `node-status-meaning`, `node-executor`, `node-verdict`, `attempt-switcher`). Then **tabs** with counts, by kind:\n- worker: Report | Files (77 · 3 flagged) | Questions (n) | Task | Receipt & events. The default is Questions while one is waiting, otherwise Report.\n- verification: Checks (gate first) | Screenshots (n) | Artifacts | Events. Default: Checks.\n- candidate: Lanes (table, failing lanes first and expanded) | Events.\n- review: Findings (blocking first) | Reviewers | Diff | Events.\n- challenge: Outcome & concerns | Events.\n- handoff/approval/integrate: a single panel (they are short), with no tabs.\n\n## What moves where\n- Worker narrative (summary, assumptions, completion evidence) appears only on the launch node's Report tab. Verify and candidate pages get a one-line \"Worker's report → Launch game worker\" link instead.\n- Files come from the worker's own freeze (`results/<lane>/1`). Files that a repair added or changed get a \"repair 1\" badge.\n- Checks, logs and screenshots stay on verification and candidate. Screenshots become thumbnails under the browser check row.\n- Findings live on review as cards. On the launch node they show only as chips on file rows, and as counts on lane cards.\n- Events: a node's events move to its Events tab (the same Log component, filtered to the node plus run-level events inside its time span). Run-level events appear in the overview Log.\n- Timing: every node header, step row, check row and reviewer shows start → end and a duration.\n- Next step: the Now banner, plus the node header of the node it concerns.\n\n## Removed or merged\nThe duplicate Nodes column (merged into the Steps timeline and the step chips), the empty node-hint panel (it becomes a caption under Steps and keeps the `node-hint` testid), the graph on node pages (replaced by the chips), the status glossary footnote, the node footnote, the empty \"Reuse evidence\" section, \"Findings on this file / No review finding names this file\" on every file, the findings legend paragraph, the app subtitle and the info line on run and node pages, and the duplicated facts in the Assignment tab.",
    "wireframes": "### 1. Runs dashboard, `/projects` (desktop 1440)\n```\nMD Manager   [Pi] [Claude] [Projects]                                              [Refresh]\nProjects                                                          ● Live · updated 3 s ago\nRead-only: runs are started, answered and approved from the workflow CLI.      (projects-info)\n [Needs you 1] [Running 0] [All 4]                                        Times: (Local) UTC\n NEEDS YOU ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n ⚑ Waiting on you   Duel core · duel-core-001                 project-B     started 11:08\n                    Launch duel worker asked question 2 of 3 · 14 min ago · deadline paused\n RECENT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n ✓ Succeeded   Skeleton review fixes · skeleton-fixes-001     project-B     10:14 · 1 h ago   32m\n               Integrated ee74298 into feature/skeleton-fixes/… (not pushed) · review approved, 2 open P2\n ✗ Failed      Walking skeleton · skeleton-001                project-B     09:32 · 2 h ago   53m\n               Blocked at Independent review · general: 1 P1 open\n ✗ Failed      Workflow guardrails · workflow-guardrails-001  MD Manager    yesterday 20:27   54m\n               Stopped at Verify combined candidate · lane ui: screenshot missing for inert-markdown\n Projects:  [MD Manager · 2 features]   [project-B · 3 features]                  (projects-list)\n```\nEach row is a single `<a>` (`data-run-id`, `data-status`, `data-attention`) to the run. On the project and feature pages the rows are identical, grouped by feature.\n\n### 2. Run overview, desktop first screen (skeleton-001, 1440×900)\n```\nMD Manager  [Pi][Claude][Projects]                                               [Refresh]    y0-56\nProjects / project-B / Walking skeleton / skeleton-001                                       y64\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Pirate Sea Race walking skeleton  skeleton-001  ✗ Failed ⓘ            ○ Finished · not polling│ y96\n│ 08:39 → 09:32 · ran 53m · feature/skeleton/skeleton-001 · automatic           [Run details ▸] │\n├─ NOW (run-now) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ ✗ Blocked at Independent review · 09:32 (2 h ago)                              [Open step ›]  │ y150\n│   Reviewer general blocked the candidate: 1 P1 open, \"Private matches can be joined without  │\n│   their code\" (apps/server/src/MatchRoom.ts:44-50). coverage superseded, no verdict.          │\n│ ┌ Next step · run in your terminal; this viewer never changes a run ───────── RUNBOOK §5 ─┐  │\n│ │ Review findings are fixed in a new run (as skeleton-fixes-001 did).                      │  │\n│ │ $ python -m workflow launch skeleton --run-id skeleton-002 --automatic --live   [Copy]   │  │\n│ └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │ y290\n│ [✓Design challenge]→[✓Launch game]→[✓Freeze]→[✓Verify game]→[✓Verify comb.]→[✗Indep. review]→[·Approval]→[·Integrate]\n│   11m · 3 tries      28m           0s        10m · 3 tries  ≈1m            ≈2m                    │ y300-380 fitted SVG\n│ ▭ agent  ┅ verifier  ┈ controller  ?                                            (graph-legend) │\n├─ LANES & GATES ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ ┌ Lane game ─────────────────────────┐ ┌ Review ─────────────────────┐ ┌ Integration ──────┐ │ y400\n│ │ Worker    ✓ worked 28m · 0 questions│ │ ✗ Blocked · 2 print jobs     │ │ · not reached     │ │\n│ │ Verify    ✓ try 3 of 3 · 5 checks   │ │ general  ✗ 1 P1 · 3 P2       │ │   approval and    │ │\n│ │           2 failed tries · repair 1 │ │ coverage — superseded        │ │   integrate       │ │\n│ │ Candidate ✓ gate passed · 5/5       │ │ ≈09:30 → 09:32 (≈2m)         │ │   pending         │ │\n│ │ Findings  1 P1 · 3 P2               │ │                              │ │                   │ │\n│ └─────────────────────────────────────┘ └──────────────────────────────┘ └───────────────────┘ │ y530\n├─ TIMELINE  [Steps] [Log]                       08:39 ──────────────────────────────── 09:32 ─┤ y550\n│ ✓ Design challenge       08:39  11m07s ▓█▓█                         3 tries · 1 interrupted  │\n│ ✓ Launch game worker     08:50  28m21s     ████████████████         stopped 09:19            │\n│ ✓ Freeze worker handoffs 09:19      0s                     |        snapshots captured       │\n│ ✓ Verify game            09:19  10m02s                     ✗✗⚒ █    try 3 of 3 · repair 1    │\n│ ✓ Verify comb. candidate ≈09:29 ≈1m06s                          █   5/5 checks               │\n│ ✗ Independent review     ≈09:30 ≈2m10s                           ██ blocked by general       │\n│ · Integration approval     —      —                                 not reached              │\n│ · Integrate candidate      —      —                                 not reached              │\n│   Open a step for its checks, files and findings.                               (node-hint) │ y860\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\nThe graph fits because dag.ts moves to node width 136 and column gap 28 (8 columns = 1,316 px). Between 760 and 1,100 px it scrolls horizontally with the focus node centred. Below 760 px it is hidden.\n\n### 3. Node view, worker lane (launch_game)\n```\nProjects / project-B / Walking skeleton / skeleton-001 / Launch game worker\n← Run · Pirate Sea Race walking skeleton · ✗ Blocked at Independent review · Next step ›  ○ Finished\n┌ sticky (run-node-list) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│‹ Prev│✓Challenge 11m│✓Launch game 28m│✓Freeze│✓Verify game 10m ③│✓Candidate 1m│✗Review 2m│·Approval│·Integrate│Next ›│\n└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n Launch game worker  ✓ Succeeded ⓘ\n Worker · agent session · 08:50:52 → 09:19:13 · worked 28m21s · stopped cleanly\n Session ended its turn: not workflow completion. Verified on Verify game, try 3 of 3, after repair 1 ›\n [Report] [Files 77 · 3 flagged] [Questions 0] [Task] [Receipt & events 3]\n ── Report ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n Worker's report · completed · as signalled by the session, not verified\n \"Walking skeleton: Colyseus server with private matches (6-char codes), 8-player cap…\"  [Show all]\n What changed  77 files at freeze (5c1a734e) · repair 1 added 2 and changed 1 · 3 named by findings\n   P1 general  apps/server/src/MatchRoom.ts:44-50  Private matches can be joined…   [Show lines ›]\n   P2 general  apps/server/src/InputGate.ts        InputGate uses an input's frame… [Show ›]\n Open assumptions (10) ▸     Untested (3) ▸\n Falsifying check  unit · npm run test:unit → Verify game, check 2      Verify yourself ▸\n ── Files tab ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n [All 77] [Flagged 3] [Markdown 6] [Repair 1: 3]\n apps/server/src/MatchRoom.ts            captured   P1×1        [Show]\n   ▾ P1 · general · open · Private matches can be joined…  [Show lines 44–50]\n     (source view, lines 44–50 marked)\n CLAUDE.md                               captured   —           [Show]  (Markdown opens Rendered)\n tests/reporters/testSummary.ts          captured   repair 1    [Show]\n assets/ship.png                         binary, not captured\n```\nWhile a question waits, the header line reads \"⚑ Waiting on you: question 2 of 3, asked 09:40 (14 min) · deadline paused, 2h31m left\". The Questions tab opens by default, showing the question and `$ python -m workflow answer <run> game \"<your answer>\" [Copy]`.\n\n### 4. Node view, review\n```\n Independent review  ✗ Blocked ⓘ\n Review · 2 reviewers, one print job each · ≈09:30:21 → 09:32:31 (≈2m10s; start inferred from the candidate)\n ┌ (review-blocked-by) Blocked by general, which blocked the candidate. coverage superseded: no verdict.┐\n │ Next · findings are fixed in a new run (RUNBOOK §5)                                                 │\n │ $ python -m workflow launch skeleton --run-id skeleton-002 --automatic --live             [Copy]    │\n └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n BLOCKS INTEGRATION (1)\n ┌ P1 · open · general · lane game ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n │ Private matches can be joined without their code.                                                 │\n │ authorizeEntry (apps/server/src/MatchRoom.ts:44-50) treats any request whose options lack `code`… │\n │ [apps/server/src/MatchRoom.ts ›]  [Requirement in game task ›]  [More ▾]                          │\n └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n [Findings 4] [Reviewers 2] [Diff] [Events 0]\n Reviewer [All 4][general 4][coverage 0]   Group by [Disposition][Worker][Reviewer]   ?\n Open (4)                                                                         (finding cards)\n  ▸ P1 general  Private matches can be joined without their code.                  MatchRoom.ts ›\n  ▸ P2 general  The full-match refusal in onAuth reads the listing before Colyseus…\n  ▸ P2 general  InputGate uses an input's frame tag only for the 30-frame window…\n  ▸ P2 general  If allocateCode fails 16 times, onCreate throws ServerError(400…\n Reviewers tab: general ✗ blocked · 1 P1, 3 P2 · file accepted 09:32:31 · launch time not recorded (print)\n                coverage — superseded after the decision · no verdict · no times recorded\n Bundle 3f2a… (candidate 0bc381f ›) · Identifiers ▸\n```\n\n### 5. Run overview at 390 px\n```\n┌ MD Manager          [Refresh] ┐\n│ [Pi][Claude][Projects]         │\n│ Projects › … › skeleton-001    │\n├────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Pirate Sea Race walking        │\n│ skeleton                       │\n│ skeleton-001  ✗ Failed ⓘ       │\n│ ○ Finished · ran 53m · 2 h ago │\n├ NOW ───────────────────────────┤\n│ ✗ Blocked at Independent review│\n│   09:32 · 2 h ago    [Open ›]  │\n│ general: 1 P1 open, \"Private   │\n│ matches can be joined without  │\n│ their code\"                    │\n│ Next · new run for the fixes   │\n│ ┌────────────────────────────┐ │\n│ │$ python -m workflow launch…│→│ (code box scrolls sideways;\n│ └────────────────────────────┘ │  the page itself does not)\n│ [Copy command]                 │\n├ LANES ─────────────────────────┤\n│ Lane game                      │\n│ ✓ Worker 28m  ✓ Verify 3/3 ⚒1  │\n│ ✓ Candidate   Findings 1 P1 3 P2│\n│ Review ✗ general 1 P1          │\n├ TIMELINE [Steps][Log] ─────────┤\n│ ✓ Design challenge  08:39  11m │\n│   ▓█▓█                         │\n│ ✓ Launch game       08:50  28m │\n│      ████████████              │\n│ ✓ Freeze            09:19   0s │\n│ ✓ Verify game       09:19  10m │\n│   ✗✗⚒█ try 3 of 3              │\n│ ✓ Verify combined  ≈09:29  ≈1m │\n│ ✗ Independent review≈09:30 ≈2m │\n│ · Approval, Integrate: not yet │\n│ [Run details ▸]                │\n└────────────────────────────────┘\n```\nTapping a step opens the node view, scrolled to the top. The step chips stick under the crumbs and scroll sideways with the current chip centred. The node header, verdict and next step fill the first screen. Findings and checks render as cards, never tables, at this width.",
    "timeline": "**Built client-side from fields that already exist.** The pure functions live in `contracts/projects/triage.ts`: `nodeSpans`, `attemptSpans`, `runSpan`, `gaps`. Their inputs are `events[]` (occurred_at, node_id, status, attempt, message), `inputs.workers[].launch.native_started_at` and `launch_requested_at`, `stop.confirmed_at`, `questions[].asked_at` and `answered_at`, `inputs.challenge.decided_at`, `max_verification_attempts`, `automatic.worker_timeout_seconds` and `review_timeout_seconds`, `results.checks[].started_at` and `finished_at`, `review.reviewed_at`, `reviewers[].launched_at` and `accepted_at`, and `summary.created_at`.\n\n**Span rules per kind** (a value derived from dependencies rather than an event is prefixed \"≈\" and carries the title \"inferred: no event recorded\"):\n- **Challenge.** Runs from its first event to its succeeded or paused event. Tries come from the message (`/attempt (\\d+)/i`, a client workaround until server/projects.ts:1067 is made case-insensitive). skeleton-001 gives: try 1 08:39:42 (no terminal record), try 2 08:45:55–08:46:41 (46s, interrupted), try 3 08:48:20–08:50:49 (2m29s, passed).\n- **Worker.** Runs from `native_started_at` (or `launch_requested_at`) to `stop.confirmed_at`, or to now while running (08:50:52 → 09:19:13 = 28m21s). Question waits (asked → answered, or now) are drawn hatched on the bar. The deadline is `native_started_at + worker_timeout + Σ question waits`.\n- **Handoff.** Its events, with failed events as ✗ markers. For guardrails-001 this shows four failures between 19:33 and 20:03.\n- **Verification.** One sub-span per try, from the \"Attempt N\" running event to the next terminal event: ✗ 09:19:13–09:20:20 (1m07s), ✗ 09:20:23–09:21:30, ✓ 09:28:00–09:29:15 (1m15s). Setup time is the first check's `started_at` minus the running event (42s). The ⚒ repair marker comes from the run-level \"Repair 1 applied\" event and the paused event #20.\n- **Candidate.** Starts ≈ at the last verify success (or the first lane check's `started_at` once lane results load) and ends at its last status event. Guardrails rows get lane chips taken from lane results, e.g. \"ui ✗ browser evidence\".\n- **Review.** Native transport: first running event → terminal event. Print transport: ≈ candidate end → `review.reviewed_at`. Each reviewer runs `launched_at` → `accepted_at`, or shows \"not recorded\".\n- **Approval and integrate.** Their event when there is one, otherwise \"≈ with integrate\" or \"no event\".\n- **Run.** Runs from `created_at` to the last terminal evidence (09:32:31 for skeleton-001, so \"ran 53m\", not `updated_at` 09:36:07, which is an export rewrite). \"Last activity\" is the time of the last event (not the controller PID line).\n\n**Steps view** (the overview default, `run-node-list`): one row per node in definition order. Columns are glyph and status, label link, start (local HH:MM), duration, a bar on a shared axis from run start to finish (or now), tries markers (✗✗⚒✓), and a one-line outcome. Bars are CSS (`left` and `width` in %) and `aria-hidden`; the times are in the text. A running bar extends to \"now\" and ticks with `useNow(5 s)`.\n\n**Log view:** every event in time order, including the node_id null ones. Each row shows local time (HH:MM:SS), a node or \"run\" chip, a status dot, and a humanised message (SHAs cut to 7 characters, \"Awaiting explicit completion signal\" becomes \"waiting for the worker to signal completion\"). The sequence number and the full message are in an expander. Consecutive \"Automatic checkpoint controller PID\" lines collapse into one \"Controller (re)started\" marker, hidden unless \"Show controller logs\" is on. Gaps of more than 2 minutes become labelled rows based on what was open: \"worker working 28m\", \"paused, waiting on the operator 5m37s → Repair 1\", \"controller down 31m ([Errno 2] 'claude' not found ×3)\". Filters: [All] [Problems]. The order is chronological, newest first while the run is live. A node's Events tab reuses this component, filtered to the node plus run-level events inside its span, so the repair shows on Verify game.\n\n**Times everywhere:** a `<time dateTime={iso} title=\"2026-09-24 09:32:31 UTC\">` element. It shows local HH:MM, adds the date when the day differs from today, and adds a relative suffix (\"2 h ago\") for last-activity and live items. A Local/UTC toggle is kept in localStorage (a per-viewer convenience) for matching CLI logs. Durations use a new `formatSpan` (3s, 1m07s, 28m21s, 2h05m). Check rows read \"typecheck · 3s · exit 0\". Attempts use one term: \"try N of max\" for verify and candidate (`max_verification_attempts`), and \"N tries\" on the challenge. A pending node shows \"—\", never \"attempt 0\".",
    "live_and_next_action": "**Classifier.** `classifyRun()` in triage.ts takes the snapshot, definition, events, inputs, review and failing lane results. It returns `{situation, focusNodeId, headline, reason, at, attention, next}`. The first matching rule wins:\n1. **Question**: a lane has `questions[].answer === null`, or `completion.status === 'question'`, or its newest event matches `/^Worker (\\S+) asked question (\\d+)/` with no later \"working\" event for that lane. The last case covers the live wait, where run-state.json is not re-exported. Headline: \"Waiting on you: game asked question 2 of 3 · 14 min ago · deadline paused\". Next: `python -m workflow answer <run> game \"<your answer>\"`.\n2. **Awaiting approval** (a node with status awaiting_approval): \"Awaiting your approval since 10:14 (12 min)\", where the time is the node's last status event. Next: `python -m workflow approve <run> --bundle-sha256 <review.bundle_sha256>`.\n3. **Challenge paused**: \"Paused: design challenge found 1 P1\". Next: edit the feature files, then `python -m workflow resume <run>`, or `resume <run> --accept-challenge \"<reason>\"`.\n4. **Interrupted, or Claude Code unavailable**: a paused or failed event whose message matches `interrupted|exit 75|Errno`. Next: fix Claude Code, then `python -m workflow automatic <run> --live`.\n5. **Identical failure before review**: a node-less \"failed identically\" log, or two consecutive failed events or lane errors with the same reason, and no review recorded. Headline: \"Stopped at Verify combined candidate (try 2 of 3) · lane ui: Expected one screenshot attachment for inert-markdown\". Next: `python -m workflow repair <run> ui --workspace`, then `python -m workflow automatic <run> --live` (RUNBOOK \"Blocked after freeze\").\n6. **Check failed with tries left**: \"the supervisor retries by itself\". If the controller is stopped: `retry <run> --phase worker|candidate --node <lane>`, then `automatic <run> --live`.\n7. **Review blocked**: \"Blocked at Independent review · general: 1 P1 open — <first sentence>\". Next: a new run, `python -m workflow launch <feature> --run-id <feature>-00N --automatic --live`, run from the target repo (RUNBOOK §5 \"Fixing findings means a new run\").\n8. **Running**: \"Running · Launch duel worker · working 5m of 3h (deadline 14:12, 2h55m left) · last activity 40 s ago\". Nothing is needed; an optional `status <run>` is offered.\n9. **Succeeded**: \"Integrated ee74298 into feature/skeleton-fixes/skeleton-fixes-001 (not pushed) · 32m · review approved, 2 open P2\". The command is labelled \"optional, outside the workflow\".\n10. **Unknown failure**: the latest failing event message shown verbatim, the step link, and `status <run>`.\n\n**Where it surfaces**\n- The Now banner (`run-now`, `data-situation`) at the top of the run overview.\n- A one-line run bar on every node page.\n- The node header of the focus node (`node-verdict`, with `awaiting-notice` kept for awaiting nodes).\n- The graph node (`data-attention`, a ⚑ glyph, amber).\n- The step chip.\n- The lane card.\n- The run rows and a \"Needs you\" count on the dashboard, once `glance.attention` exists.\n- `document.title` gets a \"⚑ \" prefix while a question or approval waits, so a background Mac tab shows it.\n- Screen readers: the existing ProjectsView announcer speaks the headline only when it changes, never on every poll. The banner is not an aria-live region.\n\n**Next step box** (`next-step`): one sentence of why, the RUNBOOK section name, and the command in `<code>` (`user-select: all`, scrolls sideways inside its own box). The Copy button's visible text is only \"Copy\" or \"Copied\", so `expectNoExecutionControls` still passes. Placeholders are shown as `<…>`. The box states once: \"Run in your terminal — this viewer never changes a run.\" `<run>` is filled from the new `RunDetail.run_dir` (home-relative). Until that field exists, the command uses `\"$RUN\"` and names the run directory pattern.\n\n**Liveness.** `useResource` records `lastOk` and `failing`. Refresh becomes a background reload that keeps the data and scroll position (useResource.ts:22-23: refreshToken moves from `base` to `token`). The LivePill shows \"● Live · updated 3 s ago\", \"▲ Connection lost · showing data from 11:14:02 · retrying\" (announced once), or \"○ Finished · not polling\". The Refresh button shows a busy state. The running glyph pulses only under `prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference`.\n\n**Wording.** Status is worded by cause (\"Blocked by review\", \"Paused: design challenge\", \"Waiting on you\"). The generic \"Marked retryable by the producer\" line is removed (server/projects.ts:1235 hard-codes `retryable: true`) and replaced by the attempt and next-step logic.",
    "evidence_disclosure": "Four levels, each one click from the previous:\n\n**L0, run overview.** Answers only, no raw evidence: the Now banner (reason, next step), lane cards with counts (checks n/n, failed tries, repair count, questions, findings by severity), and Steps with durations and outcomes. Every count links to the exact tab.\n\n**L1, node header.** Status with an ⓘ tooltip for meaning (worker: \"session ended its turn — not workflow completion\", testid `node-status-meaning`), the executor (`node-executor`), start → end (duration), a one-line verdict, the next step when relevant, and the **attempt switcher** (`attempt-switcher`) when attempt > 1: \"#1 ✗ 1m07s · #2 ✗ 1m07s · ⚒ repair 1 · #3 ✓ 1m15s\". These are links to `/nodes/verify_game/attempts/1`. The client builds `results/<lane>/<n>` by replacing the trailing number of `result_uri`, and `results/candidate_<lane>/<n>` from `lane_results`. The API already serves both (200 for game/1 and game/2). A failed attempt opens on its error and rejected checks.\n\n**L2, tabs with counts** (URL segments, ARIA tablist with roving tabindex):\n- **Checks (verification).** The gate comes first (`gate-outcome`): \"Passed · 3 gating checks; build and browser recorded here, gated at the candidate\" (`deferred-checks` as a tag). A failed gate lists each reason from `error.message` split on \"; \", keyed by the check id prefix, and links to its row. The check table (`checks-list`, `.check` rows kept) shows status, id (matched to `inputs.workers[].checks` by command), command (truncated, full in title), a derived test count where the log tail shows one, duration, exit, and a [Log] toggle. A check the gate rejected shows \"exit 0 · rejected: no passing test evidence\" in red, with its log tail opened automatically. The setup line reads \"Setup npm ci 42s\". cwd and the artifact id move into a tooltip.\n- **Screenshots.** A 220 px thumbnail grid under the browser check row and in its own tab (`screenshots`). Each thumbnail is an `<a>` that opens the full artifact in a new tab. The sha256 moves to a tooltip. Scenario captions wait for the optional packet field.\n- **Files (worker).** A dense list (`created-files`, `changed-files`, `created-file[data-path][data-state][data-findings]`), about 32 px per row: path, capture state, a findings badge (P1×1), a repair badge, and [Show]. Nothing is fetched until a row is expanded, and Markdown opens on Rendered. Filter chips: All, Flagged, Markdown, Repair. A finding link from the review opens `/files`, expands that row (`captured-file`, `file-findings`, `show-lines` kept) and scrolls it into view with the existing `keepInView`.\n- **Findings (review).** Blocking findings first, as cards (`finding`). The title is the first sentence, the rest is behind \"More\", and file:line chips link to the Files tab. The requirement quote is collapsible. A column that has one value everywhere, such as the worker on a single-lane run, is hidden. The legend paragraph moves to a \"?\" popover. The reviewer filter and grouping stay (`filter-reviewer`, `group-by-*`, `section[data-reviewer-group]` with its h5).\n- **Lanes (candidate).** A table: lane · gate ✓/✗ · checks n/n · reason · screenshots. Failing lanes are sorted first and expanded (`lane-result:<lane>`). Passing lanes are collapsed, and the \"Trusted candidate check capture…\" summary and the empty-assumptions line are dropped.\n- **Questions, Task and Receipt & events (worker).** Questions (`worker-questions`) is first and the default while one waits. Task holds the task, owned paths as an inline wrapped list, the required checks table and the exact prompt. Receipt & events holds the launch receipt, with \"State at launch\" in place of \"Observed state\" and the launcher fields hidden after the stop, followed by the node's Log.\n- **Report (worker).** The worker's completion summary is clamped to 3 lines. \"Reported by the worker\" is shown once. If the result summary adds text (repair notes), only that addition appears, as a \"Verifier note\". Assumptions and untested items are collapsed.\n\n**L3, row expansion and identifiers.** File source or rendered view with marked lines, full check logs, full finding text, and an \"Identifiers\" `<details>` holding session ids, base and output commits, bundle and sha256. Session ids appear once there, not three times.\n\n**Deduplication.** Where a verify node and a launch node share a `result_uri`, the verify node shows no narrative. The reuse section renders only when `result_reused` events exist (`reuse-list`). The empty-file findings text and the node footnotes are gone. **Artifacts** are collapsed and labelled \"Setup: npm ci (log)\" when the artifact id matches the setup ordinal. The test report attaches to the browser check row.",
    "removed_or_demoted": "**Removed**\n- The 11-fact grid at the top of the run page (RunView.tsx:98-131). It moves into the collapsed Run details, apart from what the title row shows.\n- \"Last event: sequence N\".\n- The empty \"Select a node…\" panel. `node-hint` becomes a caption under Steps.\n- The duplicate Nodes column and its 1fr/2fr grid (RunView.tsx:164-214, App.css:345).\n- The keyboard hint paragraph (RunView.tsx:161). It becomes a visually hidden `aria-describedby` on the graph.\n- The status glossary footnote (RunView.tsx:217). It moves into the status ⓘ popover.\n- The node footnote (NodeDetail.tsx:488).\n- The empty \"Reuse evidence\" section (NodeDetail.tsx:340-357).\n- \"Findings on this file / No review finding names this file\" on each of the 77 files (CreatedFiles.tsx:135-137).\n- The 4-line findings legend (ReviewDetail.tsx:323-325).\n- The Projects app subtitle (App.tsx:635).\n- The info line on run and node pages (ProjectsView.tsx:319-324). It stays on /projects for \"Read-only\".\n- The \"Result attempt 3 (graph node attempt is 1)\" wording.\n- The generic \"retryable\" sentence.\n- The repeated worker summary and assumptions on verify and candidate, and the \"Reported by the worker\" block when it equals the result.\n- The duplicated facts at the top of the Assignment tab (reduced to one summary line).\n- The pending-node dash override (App.css:335), which collided with the executor dashes.\n- The per-kind stroke colours that reused status colours.\n- The graph on node pages (replaced by the sticky step chips).\n- \"Home\" as the first crumb on Projects routes.\n\n**Demoted**\n- Session ids, commits, sha256 and bundle hash go into an \"Identifiers\" disclosure.\n- The launch receipt goes into the Receipt & events tab.\n- The task goes into the Task tab.\n- decisions.md is collapsed, with a heading outline.\n- The \"Current definition\" graph on the feature page goes behind a disclosure (open when there are no runs).\n- The executor legend shrinks to one line of three chips, with the sentence in a \"?\" popover.\n- Check cwd, artifact ids and the absolute UTC times go into tooltips (`<time title>`).\n- The 8 P2 challenge concerns are collapsed to one line each (P0 and P1 stay expanded).\n- The events list moves from the bottom of every node page into an Events tab and the overview Log.\n- Controller PID lines are hidden behind \"Show controller logs\".\n- \"Feature implementation\" becomes secondary text under the feature title.\n\n**Kept, but shorter** (truthfulness)\n- Executor marks: graph dashes and three legend entries, plus the \"Executed by\" text in the node header.\n- \"Not workflow completion\": one line on worker nodes and a status tooltip.\n- \"As signalled by the session, not verified\": a tag on the worker report.\n- Read-only / CLI-only: stated once in the Next step box and once on /projects.\n- \"≈ inferred\" markers on times that come from no event.",
    "data_needs": "**Existing fields used (slices 1 and 2 need no backend change)**\n- **Run detail:** `summary.status`, `created_at` and `updated_at`; `snapshot.nodes[].status`, `attempt`, `result_uri`, `lane_results[]` and `session_id`; `definition.nodes[].label`, `kind` and `depends_on`.\n- **Events:** `events[]`, including the node_id null ones: `occurred_at`, `node_id`, `status`, `attempt`, `message`, `type`.\n- **Inputs:** `feature`, `source_branch`, `mode`, `automatic.*_timeout_seconds` and `finish`, `max_verification_attempts`, and `setup[]`. Per worker: `launch.native_started_at` and `launch_requested_at`, `stop.confirmed_at`, `questions[]`, `completion.status`, `question` and `summary`, `checks[].id`, `kind`, `command` and `scenarios`. The challenge's `status`, `attempts`, `concerns` and `decided_at`.\n- **Results:** `status`, `error.message`, `checks[].started_at`, `finished_at` and `exit_code`, `artifacts[]`, `changed_files`, `deferred_checks`. This includes the earlier attempts `results/<lane>/<n>` and `results/candidate_<lane>/<n>`, which the API already serves.\n- **Review:** `verdict`, `reviewers[]`, `findings[]`, `reviewed_at`, `bundle_sha256` and `diff`.\n\n**Backend additions (small, and each needed for a named finding)**\n1. **`RunSummary.glance`** (optional, strict object). Fields: `{feature: string|null, focus: {node_id, label, status}|null, attention: 'question'|'awaiting_approval'|'paused'|'failed'|null, headline: string, last_activity_at: timestamp, finished_at: timestamp|null}`. The server computes it in `projectRun` (server/projects.ts:914-940), which `listRuns` already calls for every run, by calling the same `classifyRun` from `contracts/projects/triage.ts`. Without it the dashboard would need detail, events, inputs and review for every run (4N requests every poll). It resolves run-list-uninformative, hierarchy-depth, the naming findings (feature title with no extra request) and question-attention at list level. Contract changes: runSummarySchema, runList.schema.json, examples.ts and contract.test.ts.\n2. **`RunDetail.run_dir: string|null`**. The run directory as the server knows it from the registry's runs root, served home-relative (`~/.local/state/agent-workflows/project-B/skeleton/skeleton-001`). It is null when outside $HOME, as in the Playwright temp roots, or when turned off by config. redactPaths (server/projects.ts:75) rightly strips it from messages, so without this field no command can be copy-pasted, and the viewer cannot build it because the project directory's case differs from the project id (project-B vs project-b).\n3. **One-line projection fixes.** `attemptFromMessage` becomes case-insensitive (`/\\battempt (\\d+)\\b/i`, server/projects.ts:1067-1070) so challenge events carry their real attempt. The raw `controller` node is never aliased onto a lane named `controller` (341-347 vs 1116), so controller errors stop landing on launch_controller.\n\n**Optional, later (controller or exporter); the viewer works without them, with \"≈ inferred\" markers:**\n- Print-transport review start and verdict events, with `launched_at` per job.\n- An approval `status_changed` event naming the actor.\n- The PID checkpoint written as a node-less `log`.\n- The lane named in candidate events.\n- A completion `signalled_at` field, and `observed_at` for the launch state.\n- The packet's `gate.reasons[]` and `evidence.checks[]` (id, test counts, scenario → screenshot) as an optional result field.\n- Live `<lane>.questions.json` read by the server.\n- A controller-alive check from the latest PID event.",
    "implementation": "**New modules**\n- `contracts/projects/triage.ts` (~280 LOC, pure, no React). Exports `nodeSpans`, `attemptSpans`, `runSpan`, `gapRows`, `classifyRun`, `nextStep(situation, runDir)`, `laneSummaries`, `gateReasonsByCheck`, `attemptResultPaths` and `humanizeEvent`. The browser and the server share it.\n- `contracts/projects/triage.test.ts` (~220 LOC, vitest). Fixtures are sanitized copies of the skeleton-001, skeleton-fixes-001 and workflow-guardrails-001 payloads, plus a synthetic question run. The tests assert headlines, commands, spans, gaps and tries.\n- `src/projects/time.ts` (~70): `formatClock`, `formatAgo`, `formatSpan` and a timezone preference. `useNow.ts` (~15). A `Time` component added to panels.tsx (~25).\n- `RunHeader.tsx` (~110): title row, LivePill, the status ⓘ popover (a `<details>`-based popover, no library).\n- `NowBanner.tsx` (~150) with `NextStep` and `CopyButton` (~60; `navigator.clipboard` with a select-all fallback).\n- `LaneCards.tsx` (~160).\n- `Timeline.tsx` (~240): the Steps view (`run-node-list`), the Log view and the gap rows.\n- `StepChips.tsx` (~90): the sticky node-page navigation (`run-node-list`), prev/next links.\n- `NodeHeader.tsx` (~160): verdict strip, timing line, attempt switcher, next step.\n- `NodeTabs.tsx` (~90): tabs synced to the URL, roving tabindex, counts.\n\n**Changed files**\n- `RunView.tsx`: rewritten (~220 → ~210). It switches between the overview and node layouts; the facts move into a `RunDetails` disclosure; the review and failing lane results needed by the banner are fetched here.\n- `NodeDetail.tsx` (491 → ~430): sections become tab panels; ResultFacts is shown once; reuse shows only when present; VerifiedEvidence puts the gate first, adds the check table and thumbnails; LaneResult becomes a table.\n- `CreatedFiles.tsx`: dense rows, collapsed by default, filter chips, a repair diff (compare `results/<lane>/1` against the current result by sha256).\n- `ReviewDetail.tsx`: blocking cards, finding cards, the legend moved to a popover.\n- `WorkerInputs.tsx`: questions first with the answer command, receipt wording, StopLine folded into the timing line.\n- `Assignment.tsx`: per-lane table, decisions collapsed, one summary line.\n- `Challenge.tsx`: headline, collapsible concerns.\n- `WorkflowGraph.tsx` + `dag.ts`: node 136, gap 28, label wrap at 17 characters, CSS `width:100%; height:auto; max-width:<layout>px`, a status glyph and a separate `.workflow-node-duration` text (the meta line and aria-label stay unchanged), `data-attention`, a selection style that does not reuse the running colour, legend with short labels.\n- `ProjectsView.tsx`: runs dashboard, grouped project page, run rows, crumbs by feature title with a node crumb, info line only on /projects.\n- `routes.ts` (+~40): the `assignment`, `<section>` and `attempts/<k>` segments.\n- `useResource.ts` (+~15): Refresh as a background reload, `lastOk` and `failing`.\n- `App.tsx`: no subtitle on Projects, Refresh busy state.\n- `App.css` (+~200): now-banner, next-step, lane-grid, timeline rows and bars, sticky chips (`position: sticky; top: 0`), tabs, file rows, finding cards, thumbnail grid, `overflow-wrap: anywhere` on `.node-detail`/`.worker-summary` (fixes the 427 px overflow), rules at ≤760 px, `prefers-reduced-motion`.\n- Server: `server/projects.ts` gains glance (+~40), run_dir (+~20), the attempt regex and the alias fix. `contracts/projects/v1.ts` and the JSON schemas get the optional fields.\n\n**Slices** (each ships alone, with its tests migrated in the same slice)\n- **S1, \"Answer first\"** (client only, ~1,100 LOC). Time utilities, useResource freshness, triage.ts classify, spans and nextStep (commands with `\"$RUN\"`), RunHeader and LivePill, NowBanner, fitted graph with durations, Steps and Log timeline, Run details disclosure. The run page then answers what, why, when and next.\n- **S2, \"Node view\"** (~1,200 LOC). StepChips, NodeHeader with the attempt switcher, routed tabs, verify gate first with rejected checks, durations and thumbnails, worker Report and dense Files with the repair badge, questions first, review blocking cards, candidate lane table, challenge headline, deduplication, mobile CSS.\n- **S3, \"Lists and backend\"** (~500 LOC including server). Glance, run_dir (commands become copyable), attempt regex, alias fix, dashboard, project and feature pages, crumbs, Needs you badges, the document.title flag.\n- **S4, \"Assignment and depth\"**. Routed Assignment per lane; review diff rendered inline per file (a client-side patch split); changed files get A/M/D status and +/- counts from the review patch; scenario captions and gate reasons once the optional packet field lands.\n\nNo new dependencies. Everything stays plain React, TypeScript and CSS.",
    "test_impact": "**Kept testids.** run-view (and its data attributes), run-status, run-status-meaning (in the ⓘ popover, still in the DOM), workflow-graph and its data-graph-node, aria-label and `.workflow-node-meta` text, data-edge-*, graph-legend (3 li with data-executor, text still matching Agent session / Trusted verifier / Controller), run-node-list with `li[data-node-id] > a` in definition order (the Steps view on the overview, the chips on node pages, aria-current on the current node), node-detail, node-executor, node-status-meaning (\"not workflow completion\" on worker nodes), node-attempt, tab-run and tab-assignment in the \"Run views\" tablist, run-inputs-facts, pinned-definition, definition-changed and definition-current (inside run-details), worker-result (data-view), worker-summary, gate-outcome, deferred-checks, ownership-outcome, checks-list and `.check`/`.check-exit`/`.check-deferred`, screenshots img, artifacts, created-files, changed-files, created-file[data-state], captured-file, file-rendered, file-source, show-lines, file-findings, review-result, review-verdict, review-blocked-by, review-summary, reviewer-strip, reviewer-entry, review-findings, finding, filter-reviewer, group-by-*, `section[data-reviewer-group]` h5 labels, worker-questions and its children, worker-questions-waiting (\"workflow answer\"), awaiting-notice, task-panel, task-highlight, launch-receipt, worker-stop, lane-result:<lane>, lane-files-link, node-events and events-none (inside the Events tab), reuse-list, projects-list, workflows-list, run-list, projects-info (\"Read-only\", /projects only) and node-hint.\n\n**Migrations**\n- **projects.spec.ts**\n  - :138, :181, :271: the workflow crumb label becomes the feature title or workflow id. Assert the new label.\n  - :157, :184 and lanes.spec.ts:56, :153, :194: open `run-details` before `toBeVisible` on definition-changed or definition-current. Add a helper `openRunDetails`.\n  - :228: assumptions on the verify node move to the launch Report tab.\n  - :232-233: click the Events tab first. reuse-none is gone, so assert `reuse-list` has count 0 or is visible.\n  - :252: reuse-list lives in the Events tab of verify_ui.\n- **inputs.spec.ts**\n  - :143-155: launch-receipt and worker-stop are in the Receipt & events tab (click it first). Assert `time[datetime=\"…\"]` or set `timezoneId: 'UTC'` in tests/project-workflows/playwright.config.ts and assert the new \"10:00\" format together with the title attribute.\n  - :263: open run-details.\n  - :57-60: pass unchanged, because the Assignment summary line keeps the feature, branch, mode and deadlines.\n- **guardrails.spec.ts:56, :222-231**: the `shown()` UTC helper checks the `time` title or datetime instead of the text.\n- **clarity.spec.ts**\n  - executor-marks: the loop that clicks graphNode from node pages clicks `nodeListItem(page, id).getByRole('link')` instead, because the graph appears only on the overview.\n  - created-file-rendered: click the row's Show toggle, then assert that Markdown opens Rendered.\n  - output-first-task-collapsed: rewritten to \"Report is the default tab; Files, Task and Receipt are tabs; a finding requirement link opens `/nodes/launch_ui/task` with the quote highlighted in view\". The `task-details` open-attribute assertions go.\n  - findings-on-files: `file-findings-none` text becomes `created-file[data-findings=\"0\"]`; the file link opens `/files` with the row expanded.\n  - verify-shows-checks-not-files: passes with Checks as the default tab.\n- **review.spec.ts:149** still passes (awaiting-notice is in the node header).\n- **expectNoExecutionControls** (support.ts:32-36) keeps passing. Step chips, attempt chips and thumbnails are `<a>` links, not buttons. Button texts (Copy, Show, Log, Steps, Log, Local, UTC, the tab names) avoid the regex.\n\n**New specs** (tests/project-workflows/triage.spec.ts)\n- `[scenario:now-banner-review-blocked]`: focus-node link to review, P1 text, next-step code contains `workflow launch`, Copy button present.\n- `[scenario:now-banner-question]`: on RUN_GUARDED_ASKING, \"Waiting on you\", the answer command names the lane, graph and chip carry `data-attention=\"question\"`, the Questions tab is the default.\n- `[scenario:now-banner-succeeded]`: integrated commit and duration.\n- `[scenario:timeline-steps-log]`: durations present, node-less repair and diagnosis rows visible in Log, PID lines hidden until the toggle.\n- `[scenario:node-tabs-routed]`: tab and attempt survive reload; attempt 1 loads results/<lane>/1.\n- `[scenario:gate-rejected-check]`: exit-0 check marked rejected.\n- `[scenario:live-pill]`: a failed poll (mock 503) shows Connection lost and keeps the data.\n- `[scenario:mobile-390]`: `scrollWidth <= 390` on the run, verify and review pages; the node header is inside the first 900 px after a chip tap.\n- `[scenario:runs-dashboard]`: groups and `data-attention`, once glance exists.\n\n**Unit tests**\n- vitest for triage.ts and time.ts on the real payloads.\n- server/projects.test.ts for glance, run_dir (null under the temp roots), the case-insensitive attempt parse and the controller alias.",
    "risks": "- **A wrong classification misleads the operator.** This is the biggest risk, because the banner is trusted first. Mitigations:\n  - Every rule is unit-tested on the real runs.\n  - Unmatched states fall back to \"unknown\", which shows the raw failing message and the step link.\n  - The banner always links to the evidence.\n  - Inferred times carry \"≈\".\n  - Commands are templates from the RUNBOOK with visible `<…>` placeholders, and no destructive command is ever suggested.\n  - The RUNBOOK and the CLI can drift from the rule table. Keep the table in one file and cite the RUNBOOK section in the UI so drift gets noticed.\n- **Stale question state.** run-state.json is not re-exported during the handoff wait, so questions in inputs can lag. The event-pattern fallback depends on the controller's message wording. The proper fix is the optional server-side live read.\n- **run_dir exposure.** It reveals the home-relative storage layout. It is served home-relative only, null outside $HOME, and can be turned off by config. The `renderedText` assertion (no `/home/` or `/tmp/`) still holds.\n- **Contract change.** runSummarySchema and runDetailSchema are strict. The new fields are optional, and the client and server ship together from one repo. Older exports simply lack glance and fall back to a status-only row.\n- **Test churn.** About 25 assertions across 6 specs change, plus new specs. Doing it slice by slice keeps each PR reviewable.\n- **Hidden content.** Tabs and collapsed sections break Ctrl-F across a node. Mitigations: counts on tab labels, the Report tab summarising what changed and what was flagged, and finding and file links that deep-link into the right tab.\n- **Load and noise.**\n  - Dashboard fan-out (projects → workflows → runs) polls every 10 s. That is about 8 requests today, acceptable locally, and a global endpoint can come later.\n  - The overview's extra fetches (review, failing lane results, results/<lane>/1 for the repair diff) run only when needed.\n  - Relative times re-render every 5 s. Use a single `useNow` at the RunView level.\n- **Graph readability.** At 1,100-1,316 px the graph scales down to 0.83; below 1,100 px it scrolls instead. Parallel-lane layouts with many rows may still be tall.\n- **Timezone.** The local-time display can differ from CLI logs. The UTC toggle and the `<time title>` cover it. Tests must pin `timezoneId`.\n- **Partial fixes.** no-diff-view and screenshot scenario captions are only partly addressed until S4 and the optional packet fields. Print-review and approval timing stay inferred until the controller emits events.",
