    "angle": "graph-inspector",
    "name": "Pinned Pipeline + Tabbed Inspector",
    "thesis": "Every run page has two panes. The first is a pipeline band that is always on screen, fits the page width, and is also the step list. The second is an inspector below it that answers questions in the same order everywhere: Summary (what happened, why, what do I type next), Timeline (when and how long), Evidence (proof), Inputs (what was asked). The run itself is the default subject; a step replaces it when selected. Above both sits a run header whose \"Now\" line names the active or failed step, its reason and the next CLI command before anything else. Each piece of evidence has exactly one home; every other page shows a one-line link to it. The pipeline never clips, and a node inspector is at most about two screens because long lists live in collapsed, filterable tables in the Evidence tab.",
    "information_architecture": "## Routes (pathname only, extends `routes.ts`, no query strings, since App routing is pathname-based)\n| Route | Page | Answers first |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/projects` | **Runs home** | \"Does anything need me? What is running now? What happened last?\" Order: Needs-you cards → Active & recent runs table (all projects, newest first) → Project cards. The only page with the read-only note (`projects-info`). |\n| `/projects/<p>` | **Project** | Recent runs of this project, grouped by workflow. Each group title is the feature title, or `workflow_id` when names collide. |\n| `/projects/<p>/workflows/<w>` | **Run list** | Runs as rows (status, where it stopped or stands now, took, last activity). \"Current definition\" moves below the list as a small, fitted, static pipeline. |\n| `/…/runs/<r>[/timeline\\|/evidence\\|/inputs]` | **Run page, run inspector** | Header + Now line → pipeline → inspector for the run (Summary is the default and needs no segment). |\n| `/…/runs/<r>/nodes/<n>[/attempts/<k>][/timeline\\|/evidence\\|/inputs]` | **Run page, node inspector** | The same layout. The run header collapses to one line, and the inspector opens with the node's verdict strip. |\n`parseProjectsPathname` accepts a tab literal after the run id or node id, and `attempts/<int>` after the node id. The Assignment tab (component state, RunView.tsx:50) is removed, so every view can be linked.\n\n## What each pane answers\n- **Run header** (always shown; one line when a node is selected): status worded by cause, one short truthful sentence (`run-status-meaning`), how long it ran (created → last activity, not `updated_at`), a live chip and a UTC/local toggle. The **Now** block gives where, when, why and next (see live_and_next_action). One facts line: feature · branch · base · mode · deadlines · pinned revision, with `definition-changed`/`definition-current` shown as a chip. A **Run details** disclosure holds the rest.\n- **Pipeline band** (sticky): each step shows status glyph and colour, label, duration, retry and repair marks, and badges (`1 P1`, `?` question). It is the only step list (`run-node-list`), with prev/next in the inspector. The legend is three chips.\n- **Inspector tabs** (identical order for the run and for every node, with counts in the labels):\n  - *Summary*: the answer. For the run: the Outcome-by-step table (started, took, tries, one-line outcome), Evidence at a glance (counts that link into node Evidence tabs), and Needs you. For a node: the kind-specific top items (question card, gate + failing checks, blocking findings, challenge P0/P1, lane table).\n  - *Timeline*: for the run, a phase Gantt table plus an activity list that includes run-level (`node_id: null`) events. For a node, the same list filtered to that node and grouped by attempt, plus receipts (launch, questions, stop), check setup and check time, and reviewer spans.\n  - *Evidence*: full lists as dense, collapsed, filterable tables: files, checks and logs, screenshots, findings, diff, concerns, identifiers.\n  - *Inputs*: what was asked. Assignment content is split here. The **run** Inputs tab holds run facts, lanes, decisions.md (height-capped) and setup. **launch_<lane>** holds the task, owned paths, required checks, scenarios and prompt. **verify_<lane>** holds that lane's required checks and timeouts, setup, the attempt cap and owned paths (the ownership gate). **candidate** holds the checks gated at the candidate. **review** holds reviewers, transport, deadline and bundle. **approval/integrate** hold the finish policy and source branch. **challenge** holds the pinned tasks/decisions/PRD hashes and links to decisions.\n\n## What moves where (one home per item)\n| Item | Today | New home | Elsewhere |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Failing step, reason, next command | nowhere / event #20 at y≈4,600 | Run header Now | node verdict strip `node-next` |\n| Run history, run-level events (#10,15,18,19,21,22,26) | never shown (NodeDetail.tsx:305) | Run › Timeline | node Timeline (filtered) |\n| Changed files | launch_game y≈2,330-17,240 | launch › Evidence (tree/table) | launch Summary lists only files with findings or repair changes |\n| Worker summary, assumptions | launch ×2, verify ×1 | launch › Summary (report) / Evidence | verify shows \"Worker's report → Launch game\" |\n| Checks, logs, screenshots | verify y≈2,480/3,165 | verify › Evidence; gate + failing checks on Summary | candidate Evidence per lane |\n| Findings | review table + inline under 77 files | review › Evidence; blocking ones on Summary | a file row shows only a badge that links to the finding |\n| Questions to the operator | launch y≈19,320 | launch › Summary (first when waiting) + Now + pipeline `?` | Runs home Needs-you |\n| Launch receipt, stop time | launch y≈19,390 / 19,780 | launch › Timeline | Summary shows \"Worked 28m21s\" |\n| Worker task | Assignment + launch Task disclosure | launch › Inputs | run Inputs lanes table links to it |\n| decisions.md, setup, run facts | Assignment + facts grid (twice) | run › Inputs | header facts line |\n| Earlier attempts (results/game/1, /2) | unreachable | attempt switcher on the verify/candidate verdict strip (`/attempts/<k>`) | Timeline attempt groups |\n\n## Removed or merged\nThe 11-fact grid (RunView.tsx:98-131). The separate Nodes column and the \"Select a node\" panel (RunView.tsx:164-214). The keyboard hint (:161). The status-enum footnote (:217) and the node footnote (NodeDetail.tsx:488). The always-empty Reuse section, which becomes a single line in Timeline. The Assignment tab. The app subtitle and info line on run and node pages. The Home crumb. \"Last event: sequence N\". \"Graph attempt / Result attempt (graph node attempt is 1)\", replaced by \"Try n of max\". The breadcrumb becomes `Projects / project-B / skeleton / skeleton-001 ✗ / Verify game` (it gains a node crumb and a status dot on the run crumb, ProjectsView.tsx:91-95).",
