    "timeline": "**Principle:** one pure module, `src/projects/timeline.ts`, turns existing payloads into spans and rows. Two views render them: the run Timeline tab and a node-filtered Timeline tab. Durations then appear everywhere as a side effect.\n\n**Run › Timeline tab**\n1. **Phase table plus Gantt** (`run-timeline`). This is a `<table>`: one row per step in definition order, with parallel lanes as separate rows. Columns: Step | Started | Took | Tries | visual bar cell (the bar is `aria-hidden`, so the table is the accessible equivalent). Each attempt gets its own bar segment. Markers: ✗ ends a failed attempt; ⟲ marks a repair (from `node_id:null` \"Repair N applied\" #21); ⚡ marks a controller (re)start (PID logs #10/15/18/22/26); ‖ marks a pause; ? marks a question wait (hatched). The axis uses local HH:MM. Silences over 30 min get an axis break, so overnight outages do not squash the bars.\n2. **Activity list** (`timeline-event`). Finished runs are shown oldest first and live runs newest first, with a toggle. Row format: local time (HH:MM:SS, plus relative time for the last hour), step chip (or `controller` / `operator`), status dot, and the humanized message. SHAs are cut to 7 characters, and known messages map to short text (\"Awaiting explicit completion signal; idle is not acceptance\" → \"waiting for the worker's completion signal\"). An expander shows `#sequence` and the full text. Run-level rows are inline. A diagnosis row (#19 \"failed identically on attempts 1 and 2 … lane repair (RUNBOOK)\") carries a **next step** tag. PID lines collapse into ⚡ chips behind a \"Show controller logs\" toggle (`controller-logs-toggle`). The same regex catches PID messages aliased onto `launch_controller` (guardrails #5/8/11/14/17/24/29/32).\n3. **Gap rows** (`timeline-gap`) appear when events are silent for more than 2 min. The surrounding events classify them: \"Waiting for the worker 28m21s\" (#9→#11), \"Operator 5m37s → Repair 1\" (#19→#21), \"Controller down 8m06s: claude not found → restarted\" (guardrails #9→#11).\n\n**Node › Timeline tab.** The same component, filtered to `node_id` plus run-level rows that name the node's lane (\"worker/game\", \"attempts worker:game\"). Rows are grouped by attempt: \"Try 1 · 09:19:13–09:20:20 (1m07s) · failed: unit, integration — no passing test evidence\". Expanding a try loads `results/<lane>/<k>` and shows \"setup 27s · checks 40s\": setup is the try's running event minus the first `checks[].started_at`. Receipts appear as timed rows here: launch requested and native started (`launch.*`), question asked, answered and waited Xm (`questions[].asked_at/answered_at`), and stop confirmed (`stop.confirmed_at`). Review nodes show one span per reviewer (`launched_at → accepted_at`, or \"superseded\"). Challenge attempts are parsed from the message (\"Design challenge attempt N\", case-insensitive), so events #1-#7 read tries 1-3 and not \"attempt 1\". `node-events` / `events-none` and `reuse-none` / `reuse-list` live here.\n\n**Span derivation rules (unit-tested):**\n- Node span = first status event → last terminal status event.\n- Worker span = `native_started_at` (else `launch_requested_at`) → `stop.confirmed_at`, or now while running.\n- Worker deadline ≈ `launch_requested_at + worker_timeout_seconds + Σ question waits`.\n- Review, native transport: first review event → `reviewed_at`. Print transport: start **inferred** from the candidate's last succeeded event, end = `reviewed_at`.\n- Candidate start inferred from the latest verify success.\n- Approval inferred from the integrate event.\n- Check duration = `finished_at − started_at`.\n- Run duration = `created_at` → last activity. Last activity = the last event's `occurred_at` or `reviewed_at`, never `updated_at`, which trails activity by 3.5 min in skeleton-001 because of export rewrites (server/projects.ts:936).\n- Every inferred value is prefixed ≈ and its tooltip names its source.\n\n**Where durations show:** the header (\"ran 52m51s · 08:39 → 09:32\"), pipeline chips, run Summary step table, node verdict strip (\"Worked 28m21s\", \"try 3 of 3 · 1m15s\"), check rows (\"unit · 2s\"), reviewer rows (\"general 3m49s\"), and run-list rows.\n\n**Time format:** a `<Time>` component renders `<time dateTime=iso title=\"2026-09-24 09:32:31 UTC\">09:32</time>`. It uses local time, adds the date only when it is not today, and adds a relative suffix for headers, lists and live items. One `useNow(30s)` tick drives it; there is no per-row timer. A Local/UTC toggle for matching CLI logs is stored in localStorage (a per-viewer preference, wrapped in try/catch). `formatTime` (status.ts:100-104) becomes `formatClock`, `formatAgo` and `formatSpan`, and `formatDuration` is reused.\n\n**Attempts:** one vocabulary. \"Try n of max\" for verify and candidate (`inputs.max_verification_attempts`), \"Attempt n\" for the challenge, \"Session\" for workers. The graph node attempt is shown only when it is above 1, and never for pending nodes.",
    "live_and_next_action": "**Run header Now block** (`run-now`, `data-situation`). `src/projects/now.ts` is a pure `deriveNow(detail, events, inputs, review, failedResults, now)` with first-match rules. Each rule yields a headline, a linked step, when (absolute + relative), a reason line and an optional **Next** command with a RUNBOOK section. Inputs come from the run page's existing polls (detail, events and inputs every 5 s) plus immutable fetches that are cached by URI (the review result and the failed node's result).\n1. **question**: `inputs.workers[].questions[].answer===null`, or `completion.status==='question'`, or the latest launch-node event matches `/^Worker (\\S+) asked question (\\d+) of (\\d+)/`. That third source is needed because run-state.json is not re-exported during the wait_handoffs step. Output: amber \"Waiting on you: game asked question 2 · 14 min · deadline paused\", the question text, and `python -m workflow answer \"$RUN\" game \"<answer>\"`.\n2. **pane attention**: the event says \"needs attention in its pane\". Output: `python -m workflow.interactive attach-one \"$RUN\" --node <lane>` (RUNBOOK:136).\n3. **approval**: a node is `awaiting_approval`. Output: \"Awaiting your approval since 10:14 (12 min)\", taken from that node's last status event, and `python -m workflow approve \"$RUN\" --bundle-sha256 <review.bundle_sha256>`.\n4. **challenge paused**: challenge `paused` / `inputs.challenge.status==='paused'`. Output: the P0/P1 concern, \"edit tasks/decisions then `resume \"$RUN\"`\", or override with `resume \"$RUN\" --accept-challenge \"<reason>\"`.\n5. **controller stopped/interrupted**: the last event is a controller or PID-less error such as `[Errno 2] … 'claude'`, or the run is paused with no paused node. Output: \"Controller stopped: …\", then `python -m workflow automatic \"$RUN\" --live` (RUNBOOK exit-75 section).\n6. **verify/candidate failed**: the first failed verification node. The reason comes from `result.error.message`, split on \"; \" and grouped by check id, matched to `inputs.workers[].checks[].id`. For guardrails this gives \"lane ui · project-workflows-browser: Expected one screenshot attachment for inert-markdown (+2)\". If a run-level log says \"failed identically\", the next step is `python -m workflow repair \"$RUN\" ui --workspace`, then `automatic \"$RUN\" --live` (RUNBOOK › Blocked after freeze). This replaces the misleading \"Marked retryable\" note (NodeDetail.tsx:106).\n7. **review blocked**: `review.verdict==='blocked'`. Output: the blocking findings (`isBlockingFinding`) and reviewer statuses, then \"Findings are fixed in a new run\" (RUNBOOK:244).\n8. **running**: every active step, e.g. \"Launch duel worker: working 27m · deadline ≈14:12 (2h45m left)\", \"Verify game: try 2 of 3 · 40 s\", \"Review: general ✓ accepted, coverage working 3m\". Then \"No action needed: the controller is supervising\", and \"last activity 40 s ago: <message>\".\n9. **succeeded**: the integrate event message (\"Fast-forwarded … ee74298; no push performed\"), the total time, and the review outcome (\"approved by general, coverage · 2 open P2 ›\"). Optional next: `git push origin feature/skeleton-fixes/skeleton-fixes-001`.\n\nFallback: status plus the last event, with `python -m workflow status \"$RUN\"`.\n\n**Command chip:** a selectable `<code>` plus a button whose text is only \"Copy\". The command is never inside a button, so `expectNoExecutionControls` (support.ts:34-38) still passes. A polite \"Copied\" status follows the click. If the clipboard API is missing (non-secure http to the VPS), the chip selects the text instead. `\"$RUN\"` stays a placeholder with the caption \"RUN = the run directory of skeleton-001 (<runs_root>/skeleton-001)\". With the opt-in backend field B5 the command is exact. Templates live in `commands.ts`: one table that is unit-tested against the RUNBOOK wording.\n\n**Waiting states outside the header:** the pipeline chip gets a `?` badge and amber state (`data-attention=\"question\"`). The launch Summary opens with the question card (`worker-questions`, `question-waiting` kept). Runs home shows a Needs-you card. `document.title` gets a prefix (\"? Waiting · duel-core-001 — MD Manager\") so a background Mac tab shows it. `onAnnounce` fires once when the situation changes, not on every poll (the dedup in ProjectsView.tsx:380-393 is reused). The stale `launch.observed_state` is labelled \"state at launch\" and hidden after `stop.confirmed_at`.\n\n**Liveness chip** (`run-live`, `data-state`). \"Live · updated 3 s ago\". It turns amber after 2 failed polls or 15 s without success: \"Reconnecting · showing data from 11:14:02\". A failed run that can still be resumed shows \"Watching\". Succeeded or cancelled runs show \"Finished · not polling\". `useResource` gains `loadedAt` and `pollError` (useResource.ts:30-34). Refresh no longer blanks the page: `refreshToken` moves from `base` to `token` (useResource.ts:22-23). The Projects Refresh button gets the busy \"Refreshing…\" state that skills already use (App.tsx:638 vs :641). An optional backend check of controller liveness (B7) would add \"controller not running: resume with automatic --live\".\n\n**Node verdict strip** (`node-verdict`) repeats the node-specific slice: status worded by cause, `node-status-meaning`, `node-executor`, \"try `node-attempt` of max\", when and how long (`node-when`), a one-line outcome, and `node-next` on failed, paused or awaiting nodes.",
    "evidence_disclosure": "Evidence is disclosed in five levels, each one click deeper. Nothing is fetched until its level is opened, except the immutable results the Now line needs.\n- **L0 Pipeline chip:** status glyph and colour, duration, and badges only: `3× ⟲1`, `1 P1`, `?`, `5/5`.\n- **L1 Verdict strip / Now:** one outcome line and the reason, e.g. \"Gate failed: 2 checks rejected\" or \"Blocked: 1 P1\".\n- **L2 Summary tab:** only what explains the outcome.\n  - worker: question card first; report clamped to 3 lines; files named by findings or changed by repair; assumptions as a count.\n  - verify: the gate first. Each gate reason is a bullet linked to its check row. Rejected checks are red even at exit 0: \"exit 0 · rejected: no passing test evidence\" (fixes NodeDetail.tsx:191-194). The attempt switcher. A compact check table (id, duration, test count when parseable, status). Deferred checks carry a \"gated at candidate\" tag.\n  - candidate: a lane table (lane · gate · checks n/n · reason · screenshots) with failing lanes first.\n  - review: blocking finding cards and a reviewer strip with durations.\n  - challenge: \"Passed on attempt 3 · 8 P2 notes · decided 08:50\", with P0/P1 shown in full.\n  - approval/integrate: awaiting notice (`awaiting-notice`) or integrate result.\n  - `result-none` stays on Summary for unpublished nodes.\n- **L3 Evidence tab:** complete, dense and collapsed. A jump-chip row with counts sits at the top.\n  - Files (`changed-files`): a tree grouped by top directory, collapsed. Groups \"With findings\", \"Changed by repair N\" and \"All\" are filters. Each row shows path, A/M/D and +/- (from `review.diff` when present), capture state and a findings badge. **Markdown is never auto-rendered**, which ends the eager fetch at CreatedFiles.tsx.\n  - Checks (`checks-list`, `.check` rows kept): a table with command, duration, exit code and a Log toggle. cwd and artifact id move to a tooltip. The log tail of a failing or rejected check opens automatically.\n  - Screenshots (`screenshots`): a thumbnail grid (~220 px) under the browser check, captioned by scenario when B6 exists and by short id otherwise. Click opens a native `<dialog>` lightbox (Esc closes, focus returns); sha256 in a tooltip.\n  - Other artifacts are labelled (\"Setup: npm ci (log)\", \"Test report (JSON)\") and collapsed.\n  - Findings (`finding`): cards. P2s are one line each. The requirement quote is collapsible. Reviewer and worker chips are hidden when there is only one value. Cards replace the 560-px-min table at ≤760 px (App.css:408).\n  - Diff (`review-diff`): split per file, each file collapsed, with the raw link kept.\n  - Challenge concerns in full.\n  - Identifiers (session, base/output commit, bundle): one collapsed `<details>`.\n- **L4 Row expansion:** file viewer (Diff | Source | Rendered, max-height 480 with its own scroll, finding line marks, `file-findings-none` only here), log tail → \"Show full log\", finding detail.\n- **L5 Raw:** the artifact route in a new tab.\n\n**Dedup rules:**\n- A result is rendered once per `result_uri`. launch_game and verify_game share results/game/3, so identifiers appear on verify Evidence, and launch shows the worker's report.\n- \"Reported by the worker\" appears once. When `result.summary` extends `completion.summary`, only the delta is shown (\"Verifier note: Operator repair 1 …\").\n- The task lives only on launch › Inputs. Its appended \"Approved ownership and checks\" JSON folds into a disclosure.\n- Findings appear on review › Evidence. Everywhere else they are badges that link there.\n- Files changed by a repair are badged \"⟲ repair 1\" by comparing `artifacts[kind=file].sha256` between results/<lane>/1 and the latest try, so the operator's changes are not credited to the worker.\n- Empty sections are one line or hidden. \"No reuse evidence\" shows only in Timeline. \"No review finding names this file\" shows only inside an expanded file.\n\n**Inputs tab:**\n- The task shows its first section plus \"Show full task\".\n- Owned paths are inline chips with \"all (16)\".\n- Required checks are one line with scenarios.\n- Prompt and decisions are height-capped.\n\n**Earlier attempts:** `/nodes/verify_game/attempts/1` loads `results/game/1`, which is served today. Its failed try shows the error and failing checks first.",
    "removed_or_demoted": "**Removed**\n- Run facts grid of 11 items (RUNBOOK-irrelevant \"Last event: sequence 26\", Created/Updated). Replaced by the header facts line and the Run details disclosure.\n- Visible duplicate Nodes column and the empty \"Select a node…\" panel (RunView.tsx:164-214). The pipeline is the list, and the run inspector fills the space.\n- Keyboard hint paragraph (RunView.tsx:161). Moved into the legend's (?) popover.\n- The 3-sentence legend (WorkflowGraph.tsx:29-33). Replaced by 3 chips with the same testid and `data-executor`.\n- Status-enum footnote (RunView.tsx:217) and node footnote (NodeDetail.tsx:488).\n- The \"Reuse evidence\" section on every node (NodeDetail.tsx:340-357, 427/431). Now one line in Timeline.\n- \"Findings on this file / No review finding names this file\", repeated 77 times.\n- Worker summary and assumptions on verify and candidate, and the repeated \"Reported by the worker\".\n- The Assignment tab and its duplicated facts.\n- The app subtitle about Pi/Claude containment graphs on Projects (App.tsx:635), the info line on run and node pages (ProjectsView.tsx:104), and the Home crumb.\n- \"Graph attempt / Result attempt (graph node attempt is 1)\" wording.\n- Generic \"Marked retryable… through the workflow CLI\" note (NodeDetail.tsx:106). Replaced by a situation-specific next step.\n- Ownership prose on verify. Now an \"ownership ✓/✗\" tag.\n- Candidate's fixed summary \"Trusted candidate check capture…\" and the empty-assumptions line.\n- Per-kind stroke colours that collided with status colours (App.css:325-327). Pending no longer overrides the executor dash (App.css:335). The selection outline no longer reuses the running colour (App.css:337).\n\n**Demoted**\n- Session ids, commits, sha256, cwd and artifact ids go to an Identifiers disclosure or tooltips.\n- Launch receipt and stop line go to Timeline. `observed_state` is labelled \"state at launch\" and hidden once stopped.\n- decisions.md goes to run › Inputs (height-capped).\n- P2 challenge concerns become one-liners on Summary and appear in full in Evidence.\n- Revision hashes and node counts on cards become secondary text.\n- \"Current definition\" graph moves below the run list as a small static pipeline.\n- The full status explanations (worker success ≠ workflow completion, executor meanings) stay one click away in (?) popovers. The short truthful forms remain visible: `node-status-meaning` \"Session ended its turn — not workflow completion.\", `run-status-meaning` \"Did not complete.\" / \"Not complete; viewing approves nothing.\", and executor border styles plus the `node-executor` text.",
    "data_needs": "**Existing fields used (enough for slices 1-5):**\n- `summary.status/created_at/updated_at/run_id/workflow_id`.\n- `definition.nodes[].label/kind/depends_on`.\n- `snapshot.nodes[].status/attempt/result_uri/lane_results[]/session_id`.\n- `events[]` (`sequence`, `occurred_at`, `node_id` incl. null, `status`, `attempt`, `type`, `message`).\n- inputs:\n  - run-level: `feature`, `base_commit`, `source_branch`, `mode`, `automatic.{worker_timeout_seconds,review_timeout_seconds,finish,permission_mode,reviewer_transport}`, `max_verification_attempts`, `selected_workers`/`excluded_workers`, `setup[]`, `decisions`.\n  - `workers[]`: `task`, `prompt`, `owned_paths`, `checks[].{id,kind,command,timeout_seconds,scenarios}`, `launch.{launch_requested_at,native_started_at,observed_state}`, `completion.*`, `handoff`, `stop.confirmed_at`, `questions[]`.\n  - `challenge.{status,attempt,attempts,concerns,decided_at,pinned}`.\n- results (`status`, `attempt`, `error.{code,message}`, `checks[].{command,exit_code,started_at,finished_at,log_artifact_id}`, `artifacts[]` incl. `file` with `path`/`sha256`, `changed_files`, `files_not_captured`, `deferred_checks`, `summary`, `open_assumptions`, commits).\n- reviews (`verdict`, `findings[]`, `reviewers[].{status,verdict,launched_at,accepted_at}`, `reviewed_at`, `bundle_sha256`, `candidate_commit`, `diff`).\n- **Earlier attempts** use the served URI convention `results/<lane>/<k>` and `results/candidate_<lane>/<k>` (verified 200 for game/1 and game/2). A chip is offered only when its fetch succeeds.\n- Results and reviews are immutable per URI, so they are cached run-wide without polling. Only detail, events and inputs poll.\n- List levels without backend: fan out `fetchWorkflows` + `fetchRuns(first page)` per workflow (4-5 requests today, polled every 15 s rather than 5 s), plus `fetchRunDetail` only for non-terminal latest runs.\n\n**Backend additions (small, additive; ordered by value):**\n- **B4 (bug fixes, server/projects.ts).**\n  - `attemptFromMessage` becomes case-insensitive and matches \"attempt N\" (:1067-1070). This fixes challenge and candidate attempt numbers.\n  - Resolve the raw node `controller` to run level *before* lane aliasing (:341-347 vs :1116), so a lane named `controller` stops absorbing controller errors and PID lines.\n  - Both are about 10 lines, with server tests.\n- **B1 (projects contract 1.5.0, optional fields on `RunSummary`, v1.ts:36-44):**\n  - `feature` (inputs.feature)\n  - `last_activity_at` (last raw event time)\n  - `focus {node_id, label, status, since}` (first failed / paused / awaiting / running node)\n  - `attention {kind: 'question'|'approval'|'paused'|'interrupted', node_id, since} | null`\n  - Why: run lists, Needs-you and project cards without N+1 detail and inputs fetches, and feature titles instead of the constant \"Feature implementation\" (export_state.py:84). Renaming the definition is avoided because the name may feed the pinned revision.\n- **B2:** `GET /api/projects/runs?limit=20`, returning recent `RunSummary` across all projects: a merge of the existing per-workflow listings by `updated_at`. Why: Runs home in one request.\n- **B3:** `RunDetail.attention[]` computed from raw `interactive` events (question asked N, needs attention in pane) with no later answer or working event. Alternatively, keep `raw_status` and `lane` as optional fields on normalized events. Why: the question is visible live even when run-state.json has not been re-exported, and server/projects.ts:373 maps interactive→running, which loses it today.\n- **B5 (opt-in):** a `show_run_dir` flag in the projects config. When set, `RunDetail.run_dir` carries a `~`-abbreviated path and commands become copy-paste exact. The default stays redacted (`redactPaths`, :75), and the UI uses `\"$RUN\"`.\n- **B6 (optional):** `WorkerResult.gate_reasons[{check_id, reason}]` and `evidence_checks[{id, tests, scenarios[{id,status,screenshot_artifact_id}]}]`. The packet already holds both; the server drops them near :1215-1235. Why: exact rejected-check marking and scenario-captioned thumbnails. The client fallback parses the `\"<check-id>: \"` prefixes in `error.message`.\n- **B7 (later, controller-side, not viewer):**\n  - Print-review launch and verdict events.\n  - An approval decision event.\n  - Candidate `running` per lane.\n  - `completion.signalled_at`.\n  - `snapshot.nodes[].attempt_results`.\n  - Controller heartbeat or PID liveness.\n  - Until these exist, the viewer shows ≈ inferred spans labelled with their source.",
    "implementation": "**New modules (pure first, so they can be unit-tested with the repo's `tsx --test`):**\n- `src/projects/time.ts` (~110 LOC): `formatClock`, `formatAgo`, `formatSpan`, `durationBetween`, plus a local/UTC mode.\n- `src/projects/Time.tsx` + `useNow.ts` (~60).\n- `src/projects/timeline.ts` (~320): spans, attempt groups, gap classification, PID collapse, challenge attempt parse, candidate lane inference by matching event times to lane-result `finished_at`, inferred flags.\n- `src/projects/now.ts` (~230) + `commands.ts` (~90): the situation rules and CLI templates listed in live_and_next_action.\n- `src/projects/useRunData.ts` (~160): a run-scoped context. It holds the polled detail, events and inputs with `loadedAt`/`pollError`, plus a Map cache keyed by URI for results and reviews. Every tab reads from it, so switching tabs never refetches.\n- `src/projects/PipelineMap.tsx` (~280). It replaces WorkflowGraph rendering: HTML nodes (`<ol data-testid=\"run-node-list\"><li data-node-id data-status><a data-graph-node data-status data-executor aria-label aria-current>`) inside `<div role=\"group\" data-testid=\"workflow-graph\">`, with an `aria-hidden` SVG edge layer (`data-edge-from/to` kept). Keyboard: roving arrows as today. Width is fitted with a ResizeObserver. Modes: horizontal ≥ ~960 px of content, vertical (transposed DAG: rows are depths, lanes side by side) below that, and a compact mode when stuck, via an IntersectionObserver sentinel. It also has a static mode for the workflow page. `dag.ts` gains `fitLayout(nodes, width)` (~50).\n- `src/projects/RunHeader.tsx` (~200: NowBanner, CommandChip, LiveChip, facts line, Run details).\n- `src/projects/Inspector.tsx` (~230): tabs as a routed ARIA tablist with Home/End/arrow keys, verdict strip, prev/next links, attempt switcher links, and focus to an `h2 tabIndex=-1` on selection.\n- `src/projects/RunTimeline.tsx` (~260): phase table/Gantt, activity list, gap rows, controller-log toggle.\n- `src/projects/inspector/` per kind, reusing existing panels:\n  - `RunScope.tsx` (~200: outcome-by-step, evidence at a glance, run Inputs = Assignment.tsx minus per-worker tasks)\n  - `WorkerNode.tsx` (~230: WorkerQuestions/WorkerSignals/LaunchReceipt/TaskPanel moved from WorkerInputs.tsx)\n  - `VerifyNode.tsx` (~280: CheckTable, gate reasons→checks, Thumbnails, attempt results; carved out of NodeDetail.tsx:92-247)\n  - `CandidateNode.tsx` (~150)\n  - `ReviewNode.tsx` (~120 around ReviewPanel)\n  - `ChallengeNode.tsx` (~90)\n  - `ControllerNode.tsx` (~100)\n- `src/projects/RunsHome.tsx` (~220: Needs-you, recent runs table, project cards) and `RunRow.tsx` (~80).\n\n**Changed files:**\n- `routes.ts` (+45: tab and attempt segments)\n- `ProjectsView.tsx` (+150/−80: levels, breadcrumbs with node crumb, info line only on /projects, name-collision fallback)\n- `RunView.tsx` (becomes the layout shell, −150)\n- `NodeDetail.tsx` (split into inspector/*, then deleted)\n- `CreatedFiles.tsx` (+160/−90: tree/table, collapsed viewers, repair badges, diff view)\n- `ReviewDetail.tsx` (+130: blocking cards, card layout ≤760, per-file diff)\n- `Challenge.tsx` (+40)\n- `status.ts` (+60: cause-worded labels, short meanings)\n- `useResource.ts` (+20)\n- `App.tsx` (+10: busy Refresh, subtitle hidden on `.app-projects`)\n- `App.css`: +~380/−70. Adds pipeline, sticky band and tab bar (sticky turned off under `@media (max-height:700px)`), inspector, tables, cards, thumbnails, a `--warn-*` token pair for both themes, and `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` guards for the running pulse and smooth scroll. The 427-px mobile overflow is fixed by `overflow-wrap:anywhere` on inspector text.\n- Server (slice 7): `server/projects.ts` (+90), a routes file (+30), `contracts/projects/v1.ts` (+45, 1.5.0).\n- Total: ~3,000 LOC added/changed, ~300 test lines migrated.\n\n**Slice order (each ships alone, with its own test migration):**\n1. **Time and trim** (client only): Time/durations, LiveChip + non-blanking Refresh, breadcrumbs, compact legend, removal of footnotes, subtitle and info line, mobile overflow fix. This fixes the UTC-only and freshness findings.\n2. **Now header:** now.ts/commands.ts/RunHeader, facts line + Run details, question detection from inputs and event messages, `document.title` prefix. This fixes the first-screen, why, next-action and question P1s.\n3. **Pipeline + inspector shell:** PipelineMap (fit, vertical, sticky, compact), routed tabs, verdict strip, prev/next, mobile step bar. Existing sections move into tabs with minimal edits, and Assignment folds into Inputs tabs. This fixes navigation, mega-scroll, the wasted column, clipping and mobile depth.\n4. **Timeline + attempts:** timeline.ts, RunTimeline, node timelines, attempt switcher, plus the B4 server regex/alias fixes.\n5. **Evidence density:** files tree, check table with gate reasons, thumbnails, candidate lane table, review cards and diff, dedupe, repair badges, challenge compaction.\n6. **Lists:** Runs home, project and run-list rows via client fan-out, name fallback, definition graph moved.\n7. **Backend B1/B2/B3/B5 (+B6 optional),** swapping the client fallbacks for the served fields.",
    "test_impact": "**Kept unchanged by design:**\n- `run-node-list [data-node-id]` with link children and `aria-current` (lanes.spec:67, guardrails.spec:92/145/311, projects.spec:40).\n- `workflow-graph [data-graph-node]` with the same aria-label format: the anchored regexes in clarity.spec:96-100, projects.spec:150/180 and lanes.spec:61-62/189-192 stay green, and the duration goes to `aria-describedby`, not the label.\n- `data-status`, `data-executor`, `[data-edge-from][data-edge-to]`.\n- Arrow-key focus and Enter to open (projects.spec:164-168).\n- `boundingBox` x-order (guardrails.spec:100-102; the pipeline is horizontal at the default 1280 viewport).\n- `graph-legend` with 3 `li[data-executor]` containing /Agent session/ /Trusted verifier/ /Controller/ (clarity.spec:105-109).\n- `run-status`, `run-status-meaning` ('did not complete' / 'not complete', projects.spec:294/313), `run-inputs-facts` (feature, 12-char base, mode on the header facts line; inputs.spec:40-95, lanes.spec:68/195).\n- `definition-changed` / `definition-current` (header chip), `node-detail[data-node-id]`, `node-executor`, `node-status-meaning` ('not workflow completion', 'This step failed').\n- `node-attempt` (the number only), `result-none` (on Summary), `awaiting-notice` (on Summary; review.spec:149, projects.spec:315-316).\n- `projects-info` 'Read-only' on /projects (projects.spec:81), `projects-list`, `workflows-list`, `run-list`, `current-definition` (still visible, below the list), `expectNoExecutionControls` (Copy buttons contain only \"Copy\"; prev/next, tabs and attempt chips are links).\n\n**Break and migrate** (~100 assertion lines). Add `nodeUrl(run, node, tab?)` and `openTab(page, tab)` helpers to support.ts.\n1. `tab-assignment` / `tab-run` (projects.spec:451-460, inputs.spec:~40-95/263-265, lanes.spec ×3, guardrails.spec ×3) → `inspector-tab-inputs` / `inspector-tab-summary` on the run inspector. The `assignment` tabpanel testid, `role=tabpanel` and `aria-controls` linkage stay. `assignment-lanes`, `assignment-selected-workers`, `assignment-excluded-workers`, `assignment-setup`, `assignment-decisions*` and `assignment-reviewer-transport` stay on the run Inputs tab. Per-worker assertions (`assignment-worker`, `assignment-task` headings, 'src/projects', 'npm run build', 'project-workflows-browser') move to `nodeUrl(run,'launch_ui','inputs')` + `task-panel`. `assignment-worker` stays on lanes-table rows with role and check kinds (`assignment-required-kinds`).\n2. inputs.spec:56 \"graph hidden on Assignment\" → the pipeline now persists: assert it is visible, or drop the assertion.\n3. clarity.spec:101-103 exact `.workflow-node-meta` texts ('Succeeded · attempt 1 · verifier') → new format 'Succeeded · verifier' (the attempt shows only when above 1).\n4. clarity.spec 'created-file-rendered' (≈142-146) and 'file-findings-none' (≈268) → go to launch `/evidence`, expand the row, then assert `file-rendered`, the Rendered `aria-pressed` and the none-text. 'output-first-task-collapsed' is rewritten: Summary leads with the outcome and the task lives in Inputs (`task-details` removed; the `openTask` helper → Inputs tab).\n5. projects.spec:162/179 `node-hint` → `run-inspector` visible with `data-scope=\"run\"`.\n6. projects.spec:208-237 run-evidence: `checks-list`, `.check`, 'Show contents'/'Hide contents' and `screenshots` → verify `/evidence`. `worker-summary` and `assumptions` → the launch node (they no longer repeat on verify). `changed-files li` → launch `/evidence` (the list keeps `li` rows). `node-events`/`events-none`/`reuse-none`/`reuse-list` (:232-256) → `/timeline`.\n7. Candidate lanes (projects.spec:397-412) → candidate `/evidence`; expand the passing lane before its screenshot.\n8. Review specs (`finding` ×28, `finding-file-link`, `finding-task-link`, `filter-reviewer`, `group-by-*`, `review-diff`) → review `/evidence`. `review-verdict`, `review-summary`, `review-blocked-by`, `reviewer-*` stay on Summary.\n9. UTC strings (inputs.spec:143-155, guardrails.spec:56/222/231): set `timezoneId: 'UTC'` in tests/project-workflows/playwright.config.ts and assert `time[datetime=\"2026-03-01T10:00:00Z\"]` or its `title`, not the long ISO text. `launch-receipt`/`worker-stop` assertions move to launch `/timeline`.\n10. Guardrails challenge concern assertions: P0/P1 stay on Summary; `challenge-consequence` for P2 → `/evidence`.\n\n**New tests:**\n- Unit (`tsx --test`, added to `test:unit`): time.ts formatting and local/UTC; timeline.ts on the three captured payloads (skeleton-001 spans 11m07s / 28m21s / 10m02s, PID collapse, gap 5m37s, challenge tries 1-3, inferred review span); now.ts situations (review_blocked, verify identical → repair, candidate lane reason, question, approval, challenge paused, controller error, running, succeeded); dag `fitLayout` modes.\n- Playwright:\n  - `[scenario:now-banner]` one run per situation, asserting `data-situation` and `run-next-command` text.\n  - `[scenario:run-timeline]` rows include `node_id:null` events and a controller-logs toggle.\n  - `[scenario:attempt-switch]` `/attempts/1` shows the failed try's error.\n  - `[scenario:pipeline-fit]` graph `scrollWidth <= clientWidth` at 1280 and 1440; still visible (sticky) after scrolling a long node.\n  - `[scenario:mobile-390]` `document.scrollingElement.scrollWidth <= 390`; tapping a step moves focus to the inspector heading.\n  - `[scenario:live-chip]` a mocked poll failure shows the stale state.\n  - `[scenario:question-attention]` the pipeline `?` badge and the Runs home Needs-you card.\n  - `[scenario:reduced-motion]` `emulateMedia({reducedMotion:'reduce'})` means no pulse animation.\n  - `[scenario:runs-home]` recent runs sorted by last activity.\n- New fixtures in mock.ts/seed.ts: a waiting question, a paused challenge, and a candidate failure with gate reasons.",
